window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 30 SEP 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000072181","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"<b>Address A:</b> Plot No. 89, Industrial Area, Phase II, Chandigarh &#8211; 160002.<br><b>Address B:</b> Plot No. 98, Industrial Area, Phase II, Chandigarh &#8211; 160002.<br>Are these addresses likely to be the same? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>पता A:</b> Plot No. 89, Industrial Area, Phase II, Chandigarh &#8211; 160002।<br><b>पता B:</b> Plot No. 98, Industrial Area, Phase II, Chandigarh &#8211; 160002।<br>क्या ये पते समान होने की संभावना है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Yes","hi":"हाँ"},"2":{"en":"No, plot differs","hi":"नहीं, प्लॉट भिन्न है"},"3":{"en":"No, phase differs","hi":"नहीं, फेज़ भिन्न है"},"4":{"en":"No, pin code differs","hi":"नहीं, पिन कोड भिन्न है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The phase, the area, the city and the pin code 160002 are the same in both addresses<br>Address A has plot number 89 while address B has plot number 98, so the plot numbers are different<br>Hence the addresses are not the same because the plot differs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): No, plot differs.</b>","hi":"दोनों पतों में फेज़, क्षेत्र, शहर तथा पिन कोड 160002 समान हैं<br>पता A में प्लॉट संख्या 89 तथा पता B में 98 है, अतः प्लॉट संख्या भिन्न है<br>इसलिए प्लॉट भिन्न होने के कारण पते समान नहीं हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): नहीं, प्लॉट भिन्न है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000072182","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"PEACE\" is written as \"ODZBD.\" How will \"SMILE\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"PEACE\" को \"ODZBD\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"SMILE\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RLHKD"},"2":{"en":"RHLKD"},"3":{"en":"RHMDK"},"4":{"en":"RHKDC"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In PEACE every letter moves one place back: P&#8594;O, E&#8594;D, A&#8594;Z, C&#8594;B and E&#8594;D, which gives ODZBD ✔<br>Applying the same step to SMILE: S&#8594;R, M&#8594;L, I&#8594;H, L&#8594;K and E&#8594;D<br>Hence SMILE is written as RLHKD<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RLHKD.</b>","hi":"PEACE में प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान पीछे जाता है: P&#8594;O, E&#8594;D, A&#8594;Z, C&#8594;B तथा E&#8594;D, जिससे ODZBD मिलता है ✔<br>SMILE पर वही चरण लगाने से S&#8594;R, M&#8594;L, I&#8594;H, L&#8594;K तथा E&#8594;D<br>इसलिए SMILE को RLHKD लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): RLHKD है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000072183","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"DEVELOPMENT\" is written as \"EEWEMOQMFNU\". How will \"MANAGEMENT\" be written? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"DEVELOPMENT\" को \"EEWEMOQMFNU\" लिखा जाता है। \"MANAGEMENT\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"NBOAHENFOT"},"2":{"en":"NAOAHENEOT"},"3":{"en":"NAPAHFNEOT"},"4":{"en":"NAOBHFNEOT"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Comparing DEVELOPMENT with EEWEMOQMFNU shows that the letters in the odd places move one place ahead and the letters in the even places stay unchanged: D&#8594;E, E same, V&#8594;W, E same, L&#8594;M, O same, P&#8594;Q, M same, E&#8594;F, N same, T&#8594;U ✔<br>Applying the same step to MANAGEMENT: M&#8594;N, A same, N&#8594;O, A same, G&#8594;H, E same, M&#8594;N, E same, N&#8594;O, T same<br>Hence MANAGEMENT is written as NAOAHENEOT<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): NAOAHENEOT.</b>","hi":"DEVELOPMENT तथा EEWEMOQMFNU की तुलना से दिखता है कि विषम स्थानों के अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं और सम स्थानों के अक्षर अपरिवर्तित रहते हैं: D&#8594;E, E वैसा, V&#8594;W, E वैसा, L&#8594;M, O वैसा, P&#8594;Q, M वैसा, E&#8594;F, N वैसा, T&#8594;U ✔<br>MANAGEMENT पर वही चरण लगाने से M&#8594;N, A वैसा, N&#8594;O, A वैसा, G&#8594;H, E वैसा, M&#8594;N, E वैसा, N&#8594;O, T वैसा<br>इसलिए MANAGEMENT को NAOAHENEOT लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): NAOAHENEOT है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000072184","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many triangles are there in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने त्रिभुज हैं?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"23"},"2":{"en":"25"},"3":{"en":"27"},"4":{"en":"29"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The figure is a big triangle with each side divided into 4 equal parts (4 rows of small triangles).<br>Upward-pointing triangles:<br>Size 1 (smallest): 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10<br>Size 2: 1 + 2 + 3 = 6<br>Size 3: 1 + 2 = 3<br>Size 4 (whole figure): 1<br>Total upward = 20<br>Downward-pointing triangles:<br>Size 1: 1 + 2 + 3 = 6<br>Size 2: 1 (the inverted triangle in rows 2–3)<br>Total downward = 7<br>Total triangles = 20 + 7 = 27<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 27.</b>","hi":"आकृति एक बड़ा त्रिभुज है जिसकी प्रत्येक भुजा 4 बराबर भागों में बँटी है (छोटे त्रिभुजों की 4 पंक्तियाँ)।<br>ऊपर की ओर नोक वाले त्रिभुज:<br>आकार 1 (सबसे छोटे): 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10<br>आकार 2: 1 + 2 + 3 = 6<br>आकार 3: 1 + 2 = 3<br>आकार 4 (पूरी आकृति): 1<br>कुल ऊपर वाले = 20<br>नीचे की ओर नोक वाले त्रिभुज:<br>आकार 1: 1 + 2 + 3 = 6<br>आकार 2: 1 (पंक्ति 2–3 में उल्टा त्रिभुज)<br>कुल नीचे वाले = 7<br>कुल त्रिभुज = 20 + 7 = 27<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 27 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q4.jpg"]}},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000072185","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives :<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) का पैटर्न पूरा करने के लिए चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनिए:<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a rectangle carrying an ellipse and a set of straight lines that run fanwise from the left side and curve down towards the lower right corner, while the lower right quarter is left blank with the question mark<br>The missing quarter must continue the same straight lines to the right edge and the same curved arcs down to the bottom edge, meeting at the corner<br>Option C shows these lines and arcs in exactly the same directions and spacing as the other three quarters<br>The other options shift the arcs towards the corner or spread the straight lines evenly<br>Hence the figure of option 3 completes the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5_opt3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) एक आयत है जिसमें दीर्घवृत्त तथा सीधी रेखाएँ बाईं ओर से पंखे की तरह फैलकर नीचे दाएँ कोने की ओर मुड़ती हैं, जबकि निचला दायाँ चतुर्थांश प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न के साथ खाली है<br>लुप्त चतुर्थांश में वही सीधी रेखाएँ दाएँ किनारे तक तथा वही वक्र चापें नीचे के किनारे तक जानी चाहिए और कोने पर मिलनी चाहिए<br>विकल्प C में ये रेखाएँ तथा चापें ठीक उन्हीं दिशाओं और दूरी पर हैं जैसी अन्य तीन चतुर्थांशों में<br>अन्य विकल्प चापों को कोने की ओर खिसका देते हैं या सीधी रेखाओं को समान रूप से फैला देते हैं<br>अतः विकल्प 3 की आकृति पैटर्न पूरा करती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5_opt3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q5_opt3.jpg"]}},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000072186","section":"REASONING","topic":"Order & Ranking","question":{"en":"Among W, X, Y, Z and V, X is taller than W but shorter than Y. W is taller than only V. Z is taller than Y. Who will be in the middle if they stand from shortest to tallest? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"W, X, Y, Z तथा V में, X, W से लंबा है परंतु Y से छोटा है। W केवल V से लंबा है। Z, Y से लंबा है। यदि उन्हें सबसे छोटे से सबसे लंबे क्रम में खड़ा किया जाए, तो बीच में कौन होगा? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Y"},"2":{"en":"Z"},"3":{"en":"X"},"4":{"en":"W"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"X is taller than W but shorter than Y, so Y &gt; X &gt; W<br>W is taller than only V, so V is the shortest and W is just above V<br>Z is taller than Y, so Z is the tallest<br>The order from shortest to tallest is V, W, X, Y, Z<br>Hence X stands in the middle<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): X.</b>","hi":"X, W से लंबा परंतु Y से छोटा है, अतः Y &gt; X &gt; W<br>W केवल V से लंबा है, अतः V सबसे छोटा है और W उसके ठीक ऊपर<br>Z, Y से लंबा है, अतः Z सबसे लंबा है<br>सबसे छोटे से सबसे लंबे तक क्रम V, W, X, Y, Z है<br>इसलिए बीच में X है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): X है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000072187","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You are an administrative officer in a district where a planned vaccination drive is being actively resisted by a community due to widespread misinformation. What is the most effective approach? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आप एक जिले के प्रशासनिक अधिकारी हैं जहाँ व्यापक भ्रांतियों के कारण एक समुदाय नियोजित टीकाकरण अभियान का सक्रिय विरोध कर रहा है। सर्वाधिक प्रभावी दृष्टिकोण क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mandate that local police authorities forcefully compel all district residents to participate in the vaccination drive to ensure full compliance with official health directives.","hi":"स्थानीय पुलिस से अधिकारियों को आदेश देना कि वे आधिकारिक स्वास्थ्य निर्देशों के पूर्ण पालन के लिए जिले के सभी निवासियों को बलपूर्वक टीकाकरण अभियान में भाग लेने के लिए विवश करें।"},"2":{"en":"Organize collaborative community meetings with trusted local influencers to share accurate, evidence-based health information and address specific community-level concerns directly.","hi":"भरोसेमंद स्थानीय प्रभावशाली लोगों के साथ सहयोगात्मक सामुदायिक बैठकें आयोजित करना, सटीक और प्रमाण-आधारित स्वास्थ्य जानकारी साझा करना तथा समुदाय के विशिष्ट सरोकारों का सीधे समाधान करना।"},"3":{"en":"Systematically post informative educational flyers throughout the entire residential area and passively assume that the residents will eventually choose to get vaccinated independently.","hi":"पूरे आवासीय क्षेत्र में व्यवस्थित रूप से जानकारीपूर्ण शैक्षिक पर्चे लगाना और निष्क्रिय रूप से यह मान लेना कि निवासी अंततः स्वयं टीकाकरण कराना चुन लेंगे।"},"4":{"en":"Suspend the planned vaccination drive temporarily to proactively avoid potential social conflict and wait for the central government to provide additional supportive resources.","hi":"संभावित सामाजिक टकराव से बचने के लिए नियोजित टीकाकरण अभियान अस्थायी रूप से स्थगित करना और केंद्र सरकार के अतिरिक्त सहायक संसाधनों की प्रतीक्षा करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The resistance comes from misinformation, so the cure is correct information given by people the community trusts<br>Community meetings with local influencers let the residents clear their doubts and take an informed decision, which is both effective and respectful<br>Forcing people or simply posting flyers does not remove the misunderstanding, and suspending the drive leaves the community unprotected<br>Hence collaborative meetings with trusted influencers and evidence-based information is the most effective approach<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Organize collaborative community meetings with trusted local influencers to share accurate, evidence-based health information and address specific community-level concerns directly.</b>","hi":"विरोध भ्रांतियों से उपजा है, अतः उपाय है समुदाय के विश्वसनीय लोगों द्वारा सही जानकारी देना<br>स्थानीय प्रभावशाली लोगों के साथ सामुदायिक बैठकों से निवासी अपनी शंकाएँ दूर कर सकते हैं और सूचित निर्णय ले सकते हैं, जो प्रभावी भी है और सम्मानजनक भी<br>बलपूर्वक कराना या केवल पर्चे लगाना भ्रांति नहीं हटाता, और अभियान स्थगित करने से समुदाय असुरक्षित रहता है<br>अतः विश्वसनीय प्रभावशाली लोगों के साथ सहयोगात्मक बैठकें तथा प्रमाण-आधारित जानकारी सर्वाधिक प्रभावी दृष्टिकोण है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): भरोसेमंद स्थानीय प्रभावशाली लोगों के साथ सहयोगात्मक सामुदायिक बैठकें आयोजित करना, सटीक और प्रमाण-आधारित स्वास्थ्य जानकारी साझा करना तथा समुदाय के विशिष्ट सरोकारों का सीधे समाधान करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000072188","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You are leading a high-profile public infrastructure project. During a live, televised press conference, a journalist presents a leaked, out-of-context document and aggressively accuses your team of financial corruption. You feel a sudden surge of intense anger and your heart rate spikes. Which of the following actions demonstrates the highest level of Emotional Intelligence? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आप एक उच्च-प्रोफ़ाइल सार्वजनिक अवसंरचना परियोजना का नेतृत्व कर रहे हैं। एक सीधा प्रसारित संवाददाता सम्मेलन के दौरान एक पत्रकार एक लीक हुआ, संदर्भ से बाहर का दस्तावेज़ प्रस्तुत करता है और आक्रामक रूप से आपकी टीम पर वित्तीय भ्रष्टाचार का आरोप लगाता है। आप अचानक तीव्र क्रोध महसूस करते हैं और आपकी हृदय गति बढ़ जाती है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी कार्यवाही भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का उच्चतम स्तर दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Immediately counter-attack the journalist's credibility to protect your department's reputation before the audience shifts.","hi":"दर्शकों का रुझान बदलने से पहले अपने विभाग की प्रतिष्ठा बचाने के लिए पत्रकार की विश्वसनीयता पर तुरंत पलटवार करना।"},"2":{"en":"Maintain absolute silence, refuse to answer any further questions, and abruptly terminate the press conference to avoid saying something incriminating.","hi":"पूर्ण मौन रखना, आगे कोई प्रश्न का उत्तर देने से इंकार करना और कुछ आत्मघाती कहने से बचने के लिए संवाददाता सम्मेलन अचानक समाप्त कर देना।"},"3":{"en":"Take a deep breath, acknowledge the document calmly, and state that you will provide a verified, point-by-point clarification by evening.","hi":"गहरी साँस लेना, दस्तावेज़ को शांति से स्वीकार करना और यह कहना कि आप शाम तक सत्यापित, बिंदुवार स्पष्टीकरण देंगे।"},"4":{"en":"Smile broadly and laugh off the accusation as a humorous misunderstanding to show the audience that you are completely unbothered.","hi":"आरोप को हास्यप्रद भ्रांति कहकर खुलकर हँस देना और मुस्कुराना ताकि दर्शकों को लगे कि आप पूरी तरह अप्रभावित हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The anger is real, but reacting out of anger on live television would harm the project's image<br>Staying calm, accepting the document openly and promising a verified clarification by evening answers the accusation with facts and keeps the discussion under control<br>Attacking the journalist looks defensive, walking out of the conference looks like hiding something, and laughing the matter off does not address the allegation at all<br>Hence taking a deep breath and promising a verified clarification is the highest level of emotional intelligence<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Take a deep breath, acknowledge the document calmly, and state that you will provide a verified, point-by-point clarification by evening.</b>","hi":"क्रोध वास्तविक है, परंतु सीधे प्रसारण में क्रोध में प्रतिक्रिया देना परियोजना की छवि को हानि पहुँचाएगा<br>शांत रहकर दस्तावेज़ को खुलकर स्वीकार करना और शाम तक सत्यापित स्पष्टीकरण देने का वचन देना तथ्यों के साथ आरोप का उत्तर देता है और चर्चा नियंत्रण में रखता है<br>पत्रकार पर पलटवार रक्षात्मक लगता है, सम्मेलन से उठ जाना कुछ छिपाने जैसा लगता है, और हँसकर टाल देना आरोप पर बिल्कुल विचार नहीं करता<br>इसलिए गहरी साँस लेकर सत्यापित स्पष्टीकरण देने का वचन देना भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का उच्चतम स्तर है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): गहरी साँस लेना, दस्तावेज़ को शांति से स्वीकार करना और यह कहना कि आप शाम तक सत्यापित, बिंदुवार स्पष्टीकरण देंगे। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000072189","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"Two of your senior team members, both exceptional performers, have developed a deep professional animosity. Their constant bickering during project design sessions is beginning to force junior employees to take sides, splintering the department's unity. What is the most emotionally intelligent course of action for you to take? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आपकी टीम के दो वरिष्ठ सदस्य, जो दोनों उत्कृष्ट कार्यकर्ता हैं, गहरी पेशेवर शत्रुता विकसित कर चुके हैं। परियोजना डिज़ाइन सत्रों में उनकी लगातार कहासुनी कनिष्ठ कर्मचारियों को पक्ष लेने पर विवश करने लगी है, जिससे विभाग की एकता टूट रही है। आपके लिए भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता से युक्त सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त कार्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Issue a formal warning letter to both individuals, stating that their annual performance appraisal scores will be slashed by 20% if another argument occurs.","hi":"दोनों को औपचारिक चेतावनी पत्र जारी करना कि यदि एक और बहस हुई तो उनके वार्षिक प्रदर्शन मूल्यांकन अंक 20% घटा दिए जाएँगे।"},"2":{"en":"Call both individuals into a private meeting, explain the impact on junior staff, and have them co-create a professional boundary framework.","hi":"दोनों को निजी बैठक में बुलाना, कनिष्ठ कर्मचारियों पर पड़ने वाले प्रभाव को समझाना और उनसे मिलकर पेशेवर सीमाओं का ढाँचा बनवाना।"},"3":{"en":"Transfer the less experienced member of the two to a different department to completely eliminate the physical point of friction.","hi":"दोनों में से कम अनुभवी सदस्य को दूसरे विभाग में स्थानांतरित करके टकराव का स्थान पूरी तरह समाप्त करना।"},"4":{"en":"Step back and let them naturally resolve their differences, assuming that two mature adults will eventually self-correct to save their careers.","hi":"पीछे हट जाना और उन्हें स्वयं अपने मतभेद सुलझाने देना, यह मानते हुए कि दो परिपक्व वयस्क अपना करियर बचाने के लिए अंततः स्वयं सुधार कर लेंगे।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The conflict is between two individuals but its effect falls on the whole team, so the two of them must be brought together in private<br>Explaining the harm done to junior staff and letting them jointly set professional boundaries makes them part of the solution and keeps their self-respect intact<br>A punishment threat, shifting one person elsewhere or doing nothing either suppresses the issue or moves it out of sight, so the quarrel would continue<br>Hence a private meeting with a jointly created boundary framework is the most emotionally intelligent course of action<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Call both individuals into a private meeting, explain the impact on junior staff, and have them co-create a professional boundary framework.</b>","hi":"टकराव दो व्यक्तियों के बीच है परंतु उसका असर पूरी टीम पर पड़ता है, अतः दोनों को निजी रूप से साथ बैठाना चाहिए<br>कनिष्ठ कर्मचारियों को हुई हानि समझाकर उनसे मिलकर पेशेवर सीमाएँ तय करवाना उन्हें समाधान का हिस्सा बनाता है और उनका आत्म-सम्मान भी बनाए रखता है<br>दंड की धमकी, किसी एक को स्थानांतरित करना या कुछ न करना — ये समस्या को दबा देते हैं या नज़र से ओझल कर देते हैं, अतः झगड़ा चलता रहेगा<br>इसलिए निजी बैठक तथा साथ मिलकर सीमाओं का ढाँचा बनाना भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता से युक्त सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त कार्य है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): दोनों को निजी बैठक में बुलाना, कनिष्ठ कर्मचारियों पर पड़ने वाले प्रभाव को समझाना और उनसे मिलकर पेशेवर सीमाओं का ढाँचा बनवाना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000072190","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 4 + 5 = 7, 16 + 3 = 7, and 64 + 2 = 10, then what is the value of 121 + 4 ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि 4 + 5 = 7, 16 + 3 = 7 तथा 64 + 2 = 10 है, तो 121 + 4 का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"15"},"4":{"en":"11"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The rule is the square root of the first number plus the second number: √4 + 5 = 2 + 5 = 7 ✔, √16 + 3 = 4 + 3 = 7 ✔ and √64 + 2 = 8 + 2 = 10 ✔<br>So √121 + 4 = 11 + 4 = 15<br>Hence the value is 15<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 15.</b>","hi":"नियम है पहली संख्या का वर्गमूल जमा दूसरी संख्या: √4 + 5 = 2 + 5 = 7 ✔, √16 + 3 = 4 + 3 = 7 ✔ तथा √64 + 2 = 8 + 2 = 10 ✔<br>अतः √121 + 4 = 11 + 4 = 15<br>इसलिए मान 15 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000072191","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Choose the correct sequence of mathematical operators to replace the asterisks (*) in order to make the following expression a valid equation.<br>14 * 6 * 40 * 5 * 18 = 44 [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित व्यंजक को वैध समीकरण बनाने के लिए तारक चिह्नों (*) के स्थान पर गणितीय संक्रियाओं का सही क्रम चुनिए।<br>14 * 6 * 40 * 5 * 18 = 44 [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"&#247;, +, &#215;, &#8722;"},"2":{"en":"+, &#215;, &#247;, &#8722;"},"3":{"en":"&#8722;, +, &#215;, &#247;"},"4":{"en":"&#215;, &#247;, +, &#8722;"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Using +, &#215;, &#247; and &#8722; in order gives 14 + 6 × 40 ÷ 5 − 18<br>6 × 40 = 240 and 240 ÷ 5 = 48, so the value is 14 + 48 − 18 = 44 ✔<br>The first option gives 14 ÷ 6 + 40 × 5 − 18 = 184.33, the third gives 14 − 6 + 40 × 5 ÷ 18 = 19.11 and the fourth gives 14 × 6 ÷ 40 + 5 − 18 = −10.9, so none of them equals 44<br>Hence the correct sequence is +, &#215;, &#247;, &#8722;<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): +, &#215;, &#247;, &#8722;.</b>","hi":"+, &#215;, &#247; तथा &#8722; क्रम से रखने पर 14 + 6 × 40 ÷ 5 − 18 मिलता है<br>6 × 40 = 240 तथा 240 ÷ 5 = 48, अतः मान 14 + 48 − 18 = 44 है ✔<br>पहला विकल्प 14 ÷ 6 + 40 × 5 − 18 = 184.33, तीसरा 14 − 6 + 40 × 5 ÷ 18 = 19.11 तथा चौथा 14 × 6 ÷ 40 + 5 − 18 = −10.9 देता है, अतः कोई भी 44 के बराबर नहीं है<br>इसलिए सही क्रम +, &#215;, &#247;, &#8722; है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): +, &#215;, &#247;, &#8722; है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000072192","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The government has introduced a new tax policy that raises taxes on luxury items.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The government wants to discourage people from buying luxury goods.<br>II. The government aims to increase revenue through taxation.<br>III. The government aims to reduce income inequality by imposing higher taxes on luxury goods. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सरकार ने एक नई कर नीति लागू की है जिससे विलासिता की वस्तुओं पर कर बढ़ गया है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सरकार लोगों को विलासिता की वस्तुएँ खरीदने से रोकना चाहती है।<br>II. सरकार का लक्ष्य कराधान से राजस्व बढ़ाना है।<br>III. सरकार विलासिता की वस्तुओं पर अधिक कर लगाकर आय असमानता घटाना चाहती है। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Only Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Only Inferences I and III follow.","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और III निकलते हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A tax policy raising the tax on luxury items collects more tax from the sale of such items, so the government is clearly aiming at more revenue, and inference II follows<br>The statement does not say that the purpose is to stop people from buying luxury goods, and it does not speak of income inequality at all, so inferences I and III go beyond the statement<br>Hence only inference II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only Inference II follows.</b>","hi":"विलासिता की वस्तुओं पर कर बढ़ाने वाली कर नीति ऐसी वस्तुओं की बिक्री से अधिक कर वसूलती है, अतः सरकार का लक्ष्य स्पष्टतः अधिक राजस्व है और निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br>कथन यह नहीं कहता कि उद्देश्य लोगों को विलासिता की वस्तुएँ खरीदने से रोकना है, और आय असमानता की बात भी नहीं करता, अतः निष्कर्ष I और III कथन से आगे बढ़ जाते हैं<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000072193","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"If a mirror is placed on the line PQ, which figure will be the mirror image of the question figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि दर्पण PQ रेखा पर रखा जाए, तो प्रश्न आकृति का दर्पण प्रतिबिंब कौन-सी आकृति होगी?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"With the mirror on the right of the figure, the combination f j 5 W 2 r is reversed in order and each character is flipped horizontally at the same height<br>So the mirror image must read from the flipped r, then 2, W, 5, j and finally the flipped f<br>Only the second option keeps this exact order with every character properly flipped, while the others change the position of the last two characters or turn a character upright<br>Hence the second option is the correct mirror image<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"दर्पण आकृति के दाईं ओर होने पर संयोजन f j 5 W 2 r का क्रम उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक अक्षर उसी ऊँचाई पर क्षैतिज रूप से पलटता है<br>अतः दर्पण प्रतिबिंब पलटे हुए r से शुरू होकर 2, W, 5, j तथा अंत में पलटे हुए f तक पढ़ा जाना चाहिए<br>केवल दूसरे विकल्प में यही क्रम है और प्रत्येक अक्षर ठीक से पलटा है, जबकि अन्य विकल्प अंतिम दो अक्षरों का स्थान बदल देते हैं या किसी अक्षर को सीधा कर देते हैं<br>अतः दूसरा विकल्प सही दर्पण प्रतिबिंब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000072194","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During a school field trip, you're a chaperone and notice that one student seems to be deliberately excluded from group activities by their peers, though no one says anything overtly unkind. What should you do? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"स्कूल भ्रमण के दौरान आप अभिभावक-सहायक हैं और देखते हैं कि साथियों द्वारा एक विद्यार्थी को जानबूझकर समूह गतिविधियों से बाहर रखा जा रहा है, यद्यपि कोई भी खुलेआम निर्दयी बात नहीं कहता। आपको क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Wait to see if the situation resolves on its own, since no rules are technically being broken.","hi":"प्रतीक्षा करना कि स्थिति स्वयं सुलझ जाए, क्योंकि तकनीकी रूप से कोई नियम नहीं तोड़ा जा रहा।"},"2":{"en":"Check in privately, offer help joining a group, and encourage inclusion.","hi":"निजी रूप से पूछताछ करना, समूह में शामिल होने में सहायता देना और समावेशन को प्रोत्साहित करना।"},"3":{"en":"Immediately separate the group of students who are excluding the other student as a punishment.","hi":"बहिष्कार करने वाले विद्यार्थियों के समूह को दंडस्वरूप तुरंत अलग करना।"},"4":{"en":"Report the entire group to the school administration for bullying.","hi":"पूरे समूह की शिकायत दादागिरी के लिए स्कूल प्रशासन से करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Silent exclusion still hurts a child, so waiting for the situation to settle leaves the student alone<br>A quiet private check, help in joining a group and a clear push for inclusion protect the child without blaming anyone in public<br>Punishing the group or reporting everybody at once creates conflict and does not teach the students to include others<br>Hence checking in privately and encouraging inclusion is the right action<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Check in privately, offer help joining a group, and encourage inclusion.</b>","hi":"चुपचाप बहिष्कार भी बच्चे को चोट पहुँचाता है, अतः स्थिति के स्वयं सुलझने की प्रतीक्षा विद्यार्थी को अकेला छोड़ देती है<br>निजी रूप से चुपचाप पूछताछ, समूह में शामिल होने में सहायता तथा समावेशन को स्पष्ट प्रोत्साहन सार्वजनिक रूप से किसी को दोष दिए बिना बच्चे की रक्षा करता है<br>समूह को दंड देना या सबकी शिकायत एक साथ करना टकराव पैदा करता है और विद्यार्थियों को दूसरों को शामिल करना नहीं सिखाता<br>अतः निजी रूप से पूछताछ करना और समावेशन को प्रोत्साहित करना सही कार्य है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): निजी रूप से पूछताछ करना, समूह में शामिल होने में सहायता देना और समावेशन को प्रोत्साहित करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000072195","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br>Question Figures:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q15.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]<br>Answer Figures: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। तीसरी तथा चौथी आकृति के बीच वही संबंध स्थापित करने के लिए दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर रखिए।<br>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q15.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]<br>उत्तर आकृतियाँ: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the first pair the two dots that were outside the figure move to the top and bottom of the figure on the same vertical line, and the shape itself is closed by joining the open ends<br>So the change is that the outer dots become attached at the two ends of the figure and the figure becomes complete<br>In answer figure 2 the two dots sit at the top and bottom of the closed shape, exactly as in the second question figure<br>Hence answer figure 2 replaces the question mark<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2.</b>","hi":"पहले युग्म में आकृति के बाहर के दो बिंदु उसी ऊर्ध्व रेखा पर आकृति के ऊपर तथा नीचे आ जाते हैं, और खुले सिरों को जोड़कर आकृति पूरी कर दी जाती है<br>अतः परिवर्तन यह है कि बाहरी बिंदु आकृति के दोनों सिरों पर जुड़ जाते हैं और आकृति पूर्ण हो जाती है<br>उत्तर आकृति 2 में दोनों बिंदु बंद आकृति के ऊपर तथा नीचे हैं, ठीक दूसरी प्रश्न आकृति की तरह<br>इसलिए उत्तर आकृति 2 प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न के स्थान पर आएगी<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q15.jpg"]}},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000072196","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br>Question Figures:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]<br>Answer Figures: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। तीसरी तथा चौथी आकृति के बीच वही संबंध स्थापित करने के लिए दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर रखिए।<br>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]<br>उत्तर आकृतियाँ: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"4"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the first pair the two small circles that were at the outer ends of the star move inside the two lower triangles and the star is inverted<br>So the change is that the outer circles become filled shapes inside the lower part of the figure while the upper part stays plain<br>Answer figure 1 shows the inverted figure with the dark circles inside the two lower triangles, matching the second question figure<br>Hence answer figure 1 replaces the question mark<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"पहले युग्म में तारे के बाहरी सिरों पर के दो छोटे वृत्त नीचे के दो त्रिभुजों के भीतर आ जाते हैं और तारा उलट जाता है<br>अतः परिवर्तन यह है कि बाहरी वृत्त आकृति के निचले भाग के भीतर भरे आकार बन जाते हैं जबकि ऊपरी भाग सादा रहता है<br>उत्तर आकृति 1 में उलटी आकृति के नीचे के दोनों त्रिभुजों में काला वृत्त है, जो दूसरी प्रश्न आकृति से मेल खाता है<br>इसलिए उत्तर आकृति 1 प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न के स्थान पर आएगी<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q16.jpg"]}},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000072197","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Identify the Venn diagram that represents the relationship between \"Taxpayers, Females, and Billionaires\". [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"उस वेन आरेख को पहचानिए जो \"करदाता, महिलाएँ तथा अरबपति\" के बीच संबंध दर्शाता है। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Some taxpayers are females and some females are taxpayers, so these two circles must overlap<br>A billionaire can be a taxpayer, can be a female, or may be neither of the two, so the third circle must also cut both of the other circles<br>Only the fourth diagram shows three circles intersecting one another in such a way that every circle partly overlaps the other two<br>Hence the fourth diagram represents the relationship<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-10-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"कुछ करदाता महिलाएँ हैं और कुछ महिलाएँ करदाता हैं, अतः ये दो वृत्त परस्पर कटते हैं<br>कोई अरबपति करदाता हो सकता है, महिला हो सकता है, या दोनों में से कोई नहीं, अतः तीसरा वृत्त भी दोनों वृत्तों को काटना चाहिए<br>केवल चौथा आरेख तीन वृत्तों को इस प्रकार दर्शाता है कि प्रत्येक वृत्त आंशिक रूप से अन्य दो को काटता है<br>इसलिए चौथा आरेख संबंध दर्शाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-10-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18_opt3.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18_opt1.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-10-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18_opt1.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-10-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-10-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18_opt4.jpg"]}},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000072198","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>To reduce the backlog of pending legal cases, the high court has decided to implement an automated digital filing system.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. The entire backlog is caused solely by the manual filing of paper documents.<br>II. All lawyers and judges in the court are already experts in using digital filing systems. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिया गया कथन तथा उस पर आधारित अवधारणाएँ ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सी अवधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>लंबित मुकदमों का बोझ घटाने के लिए उच्च न्यायालय ने स्वचालित डिजिटल फाइलिंग प्रणाली लागू करने का निर्णय लिया है।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. पूरा बैकलॉग केवल कागज़ी दस्तावेज़ों की मैनुअल फाइलिंग के कारण है।<br>II. न्यायालय के सभी वकील तथा न्यायाधीश पहले से ही डिजिटल फाइलिंग प्रणाली के विशेषज्ञ हैं। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा II निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा I निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement only says that a digital filing system has been chosen to reduce the backlog, and it does not claim that manual paper filing is the only cause, so the word solely makes assumption I too strong<br>It also does not claim that every lawyer and judge is already an expert in digital filing, so assumption II is not implicit either<br>Hence neither assumption I nor II is implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit.</b>","hi":"कथन केवल यह कहता है कि बैकलॉग घटाने के लिए डिजिटल फाइलिंग प्रणाली चुनी गई है, और यह नहीं कहता कि कागज़ी मैनुअल फाइलिंग ही एकमात्र कारण है, अतः 'केवल' शब्द अवधारणा I को अत्यधिक बना देता है<br>यह यह भी नहीं कहता कि हर वकील और न्यायाधीश पहले से डिजिटल फाइलिंग के विशेषज्ञ हैं, अतः अवधारणा II भी निहित नहीं है<br>इसलिए न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000072199","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"Four different positions of the same dice are shown. Select the number that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '4'.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक ही पासे की चार भिन्न स्थितियाँ दिखाई गई हैं। वह संख्या चुनिए जो '4' दर्शाने वाले फलक के विपरीत होगी।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the four positions of the cube the numbers adjacent to 4 are read off: in the fourth position 4 lies between 3 and 2, in the first position 1 is above 5 and in the third position 1 is next to 3<br>Collecting the faces that touch 4 gives 1, 2 and 3, so the faces left for the opposite sides are 4 with 5 and 6 with the remaining face<br>Since 5 never appears next to 4 in any of the four views, 5 is the face opposite 4<br>Hence the number opposite 4 is 5<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 5.</b>","hi":"पासे की चार स्थितियों से 4 के निकटवर्ती फलक पढ़े जाते हैं: चौथी स्थिति में 4, 3 और 2 के बीच है, पहली स्थिति में 5 के ऊपर 1 है तथा तीसरी स्थिति में 1, 3 के पास है<br>4 को छूने वाले फलक 1, 2 तथा 3 मिलते हैं, अतः विपरीत जोड़ों के लिए 4 के साथ 5 तथा 6 के साथ शेष फलक बचता है<br>चूँकि चारों दृश्यों में 5 कभी 4 के पास नहीं आता, अतः 5, 4 के विपरीत फलक है<br>इसलिए 4 के विपरीत संख्या 5 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg"]}},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000072200","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c), (d) तथा (e) से अंकित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी प्रकार समान हैं। परंतु एक आकृति अन्य चार जैसी नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो शेष से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"a"},"2":{"en":"c"},"3":{"en":"d"},"4":{"en":"e"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Every figure is a square cut by both diagonals into four parts, with one part dark and a small dot placed at the centre<br>In figures (a), (b), (d) and (e) the dark part is a whole quarter of the square that lies along one side<br>In figure (c) the dark part is a quarter formed by the centre lines and the shading is placed in the wrong way, so the figure is not like the others<br>Hence figure (c) is different from the rest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): c.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक आकृति एक वर्ग है जो दोनों विकर्णों से चार भागों में बँटा है, जिसमें एक भाग काला है और केंद्र पर एक छोटा बिंदु है<br>आकृति (a), (b), (d) तथा (e) में काला भाग वर्ग का पूरा एक चतुर्थांश है जो किसी एक भुजा के साथ है<br>आकृति (c) में काला भाग केंद्र रेखाओं से बना चतुर्थांश है और छायांकन गलत प्रकार से है, अतः यह आकृति अन्य जैसी नहीं है<br>इसलिए आकृति (c) शेष से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): c है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q20.jpg"]}},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000072201","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c), (d) तथा (e) से अंकित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी प्रकार समान हैं। परंतु एक आकृति अन्य चार जैसी नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो शेष से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"c"},"2":{"en":"a"},"3":{"en":"b"},"4":{"en":"e"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Each figure shows a hexagon with a small dark dot inside and a curved arrow outside it<br>In figures (a), (b), (d) and (e) the arrow starts at one corner and its head turns towards the dot inside the hexagon<br>In figure (c) the arrow head points away from the hexagon, so the relation between the arrow and the dot is reversed<br>Hence figure (c) is different from the rest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): c.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक आकृति में एक षट्भुज है जिसके भीतर छोटा काला बिंदु है और बाहर एक वक्र तीर है<br>आकृति (a), (b), (d) तथा (e) में तीर एक कोने से शुरू होकर उसका सिरा षट्भुज के भीतर बिंदु की ओर मुड़ता है<br>आकृति (c) में तीर का सिरा षट्भुज से बाहर की ओर है, अतः तीर और बिंदु के बीच संबंध उलटा है<br>इसलिए आकृति (c) शेष से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): c है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q21.jpg"]}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000072202","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">56</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">132</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">115</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">81</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">256</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">180</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">120</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">243</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1024</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">508</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से जुड़े/संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">पंक्तियाँ</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">56</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">132</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">115</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">81</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">256</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">180</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">120</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">243</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1024</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">508</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns I, II and III","hi":"स्तंभ I, II तथा III"},"2":{"en":"Columns I, II and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, II तथा IV"},"3":{"en":"Columns II, IV and V","hi":"स्तंभ II, IV तथा V"},"4":{"en":"Columns I, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, III तथा IV"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Column I runs 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, which is doubled at every step ✔<br>Column III runs 3, 9, 27, 81, 243, which is multiplied by 3 at every step ✔<br>Column IV runs 4, 16, 64, 256, 1024, which is multiplied by 4 at every step ✔<br>Columns II and V do not follow one fixed multiplier, so they are not related in this way<br>Hence columns I, III and IV are related with each other<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Columns I, III and IV.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ I में 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 है, जो प्रत्येक चरण में दो गुना होता है ✔<br>स्तंभ III में 3, 9, 27, 81, 243 है, जो प्रत्येक चरण में 3 से गुणा होता है ✔<br>स्तंभ IV में 4, 16, 64, 256, 1024 है, जो प्रत्येक चरण में 4 से गुणा होता है ✔<br>स्तंभ II तथा V में कोई निश्चित गुणक नहीं है, अतः वे इस प्रकार संबंधित नहीं हैं<br>इसलिए स्तंभ I, III तथा IV परस्पर संबंधित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): स्तंभ I, III तथा IV है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000072203","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Carefully observe Figure (X) and identify the option figure in which Figure (X) is embedded exactly as shown.<br>Figure X:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) को ध्यान से देखिए और वह विकल्प आकृति पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) ठीक वैसी ही अंतर्निहित है।<br>आकृति X:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a shape made of two straight lines that meet at a point on the left and open out to the right, like a lying V or a fork<br>Such a shape can be found only where two straight lines meet at a single point and go apart in the same direction<br>The second option, the square with both diagonals drawn inside it, contains exactly this pair of lines meeting at the centre and opening to the right<br>The other options have triangles, a single slanting line or parallel lines, which do not give this shape<br>Hence figure (X) is embedded in the second option<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) दो सीधी रेखाओं से बनी है जो बाईं ओर एक बिंदु पर मिलकर दाईं ओर खुलती हैं, जैसे लेटा हुआ V या काँटा<br>ऐसी आकृति वहीं मिल सकती है जहाँ दो सीधी रेखाएँ एक बिंदु पर मिलकर उसी दिशा में अलग होती हैं<br>दूसरे विकल्प में, जो भीतर दोनों विकर्णों वाला वर्ग है, ठीक यही रेखा-युग्म केंद्र पर मिलकर दाईं ओर खुलता है<br>अन्य विकल्पों में त्रिभुज, एक तिर्यक रेखा या समांतर रेखाएँ हैं, जो यह आकृति नहीं देतीं<br>अतः आकृति (X) दूसरे विकल्प में अंतर्निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q23_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000072204","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks ( _ ) using one of the following four options such that the series follows a specific pattern in the given order.<br>p _ rt _ srtps _ tp _ rt [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अग्रलिखित चार विकल्पों में से एक का प्रयोग करके रिक्त स्थान ( _ ) भरिए ताकि श्रेणी दिए गए क्रम में एक विशिष्ट पैटर्न का पालन करे।<br>p _ rt _ srtps _ tp _ rt [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"prps"},"2":{"en":"sprs"},"3":{"en":"srtp"},"4":{"en":"prst"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Filling the blanks with s, p, r and s gives p s r t p s r t p s r t, that is the block p s r t repeated again and again from the first letter ✔<br>The other options break this repetition within the first block, for example prps gives p p r t p s r t, which does not repeat<br>So the correct set of letters is sprs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): sprs.</b>","hi":"s, p, r तथा s भरने से p s r t p s r t p s r t मिलता है, अर्थात् ब्लॉक p s r t पहले अक्षर से ही बार-बार दोहराता है ✔<br>अन्य विकल्प पहले ही ब्लॉक में यह पुनरावृत्ति तोड़ देते हैं, जैसे prps से p p r t p s r t मिलता है, जो दोहराता नहीं<br>अतः अक्षरों का सही समूह sprs है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): sprs है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000072205","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Select a figure from amongst the Answer Figures which will continue the same series as established by the Problem Figures.<br>Problem Figures:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]<br>Answer Figures: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"उन उत्तर आकृतियों में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो समस्या आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित उसी श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाएगी।<br>समस्या आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]<br>उत्तर आकृतियाँ: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In every problem figure the outer square contains a circle with two lines and a small dark dot, and the dot changes from one corner to the next in a fixed order<br>Following the movement of the dot through the five problem figures, the next figure must carry the dot in the lower left position of the circle<br>Answer figure B shows the same circle and lines with the dot exactly at this position, while the other answer figures place the dot in the wrong corner or change the lines<br>Hence answer figure B continues the series<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): B.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक समस्या आकृति में बाहरी वर्ग के भीतर एक वृत्त है जिसमें दो रेखाएँ तथा एक छोटा काला बिंदु है, और बिंदु एक निश्चित क्रम में एक कोने से दूसरे कोने पर जाता है<br>पाँच समस्या आकृतियों में बिंदु की गति देखने पर अगली आकृति में बिंदु वृत्त के निचले बाएँ स्थान पर होना चाहिए<br>उत्तर आकृति B में वही वृत्त और रेखाएँ हैं तथा बिंदु ठीक इसी स्थान पर है, जबकि अन्य उत्तर आकृतियाँ बिंदु को गलत कोने में रखती हैं या रेखाएँ बदल देती हैं<br>अतः उत्तर आकृति B श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): B है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q25.jpg"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000072206","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Fundamental Rights","question":{"en":"The Father of the Indian Constitution, Dr. B.R. Ambedkar, termed which right as the \"Heart and Soul\" of the Constitution? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के जनक डॉ. बी.आर. अंबेडकर ने किस अधिकार को संविधान का \"हृदय और आत्मा\" कहा था? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Right to economic and social equality","hi":"आर्थिक और सामाजिक समानता का अधिकार"},"2":{"en":"Right to freedom","hi":"स्वतंत्रता का अधिकार"},"3":{"en":"Right to constitutional remedies","hi":"संवैधानिक उपचारों का अधिकार"},"4":{"en":"Right to religious freedom","hi":"धार्मिक स्वतंत्रता का अधिकार"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Right to constitutional remedies</b><br>Dr. Ambedkar called <b><u>Article 32 – Right to Constitutional Remedies</u></b> the \"heart and soul\" of the Constitution, because it lets a citizen move the Supreme Court directly when Fundamental Rights are violated.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Under Art. 32 the Supreme Court issues five writs: <b>Habeas Corpus, Mandamus, Prohibition, Certiorari and Quo Warranto</b>.<br>• High Courts issue writs under <b>Article 226</b>, which is wider in scope.<br>• Right to Equality – Arts. 14–18; Right to Freedom – Arts. 19–22; Freedom of Religion – Arts. 25–28.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – संवैधानिक उपचारों का अधिकार</b><br>डॉ. अंबेडकर ने <b><u>अनुच्छेद 32 – संवैधानिक उपचारों का अधिकार</u></b> को संविधान का \"हृदय और आत्मा\" कहा, क्योंकि इसके द्वारा मौलिक अधिकारों के उल्लंघन पर नागरिक सीधे सर्वोच्च न्यायालय जा सकता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अनु. 32 के तहत सर्वोच्च न्यायालय पाँच रिट जारी करता है: <b>बंदी प्रत्यक्षीकरण (Habeas Corpus), परमादेश (Mandamus), प्रतिषेध (Prohibition), उत्प्रेषण (Certiorari) और अधिकार पृच्छा (Quo Warranto)</b>।<br>• उच्च न्यायालय <b>अनुच्छेद 226</b> के तहत रिट जारी करते हैं, जिसका दायरा अधिक व्यापक है।<br>• समता का अधिकार – अनु. 14–18; स्वतंत्रता का अधिकार – अनु. 19–22; धार्मिक स्वतंत्रता – अनु. 25–28।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000072207","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"The Inter-State Council is established under which Article of the Constitution? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अंतर-राज्य परिषद संविधान के किस अनुच्छेद के तहत स्थापित की जाती है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 262 of the Indian Constitution","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 262"},"2":{"en":"Article 263 of the Indian Constitution","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 263"},"3":{"en":"Article 280 of the Indian Constitution","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 280"},"4":{"en":"Article 243 of the Indian Constitution","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 243"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Article 263 of the Indian Constitution</b><br><b><u>Article 263</u></b> empowers the President to set up an <b>Inter-State Council</b> to inquire into and advise on disputes and matters of common interest between States and the Centre.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It was set up in <b>1990</b> on the recommendation of the <b>Sarkaria Commission</b>; chaired by the Prime Minister.<br>• <b>Article 262</b> – adjudication of inter-state river water disputes.<br>• <b>Article 280</b> – Finance Commission; <b>Article 243</b> – definitions for Panchayats (Part IX).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 263</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 263</u></b> राष्ट्रपति को राज्यों और केंद्र के बीच विवादों तथा साझा हितों के विषयों पर जाँच और सलाह के लिए <b>अंतर-राज्य परिषद</b> गठित करने का अधिकार देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसका गठन <b>1990</b> में <b>सरकारिया आयोग</b> की सिफारिश पर हुआ; अध्यक्ष प्रधानमंत्री।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 262</b> – अंतर-राज्यीय नदी जल विवादों का न्यायनिर्णयन।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 280</b> – वित्त आयोग (Finance Commission); <b>अनुच्छेद 243</b> – पंचायतों से संबंधित परिभाषाएँ (भाग IX)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000072208","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"When it is midnight at the IST meridian, a place observes 6 a.m. Calculate meridian of that place. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जब IST याम्योत्तर पर मध्यरात्रि होती है, तब किसी स्थान पर सुबह के 6 बजते हैं। उस स्थान का याम्योत्तर ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"277°31′ E"},"2":{"en":"172°30′ E"},"3":{"en":"37°30′ E"},"4":{"en":"127°30′ W"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 172°30′ E</b><br>The place is <b>6 hours ahead</b> of IST, so it lies east of 82°30′ E.<br>1 hour = 15°, so 6 hours = 90°.<br>Meridian = 82°30′ + 90° = <b><u>172°30′ E</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• IST meridian is <b>82°30′ E</b>, passing near <b>Mirzapur (Uttar Pradesh)</b>; IST = GMT + 5:30.<br>• The Earth rotates <b>15° per hour</b>, i.e., <b>1° in 4 minutes</b>.<br>• Places to the <b>east</b> are ahead in time; places to the <b>west</b> are behind.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 172°30′ E</b><br>वह स्थान IST से <b>6 घंटे आगे</b> है, इसलिए वह 82°30′ पूर्व के पूर्व में स्थित है।<br>1 घंटा = 15°, अतः 6 घंटे = 90°।<br>याम्योत्तर = 82°30′ + 90° = <b><u>172°30′ पूर्व</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• IST याम्योत्तर <b>82°30′ पूर्व</b> है, जो <b>मिर्ज़ापुर (उत्तर प्रदेश)</b> के निकट से गुजरता है; IST = GMT + 5:30।<br>• पृथ्वी <b>प्रति घंटे 15°</b> घूमती है, अर्थात् <b>4 मिनट में 1°</b>।<br>• <b>पूर्व</b> के स्थान समय में आगे और <b>पश्चिम</b> के स्थान पीछे होते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000072209","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Parliament","question":{"en":"Which article of the Indian Constitution empowers Parliament to determine the salaries and allowances of its members? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का कौन-सा अनुच्छेद संसद को अपने सदस्यों के वेतन और भत्ते निर्धारित करने का अधिकार देता है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 102","hi":"अनुच्छेद 102"},"2":{"en":"Article 104","hi":"अनुच्छेद 104"},"3":{"en":"Article 106","hi":"अनुच्छेद 106"},"4":{"en":"Article 108","hi":"अनुच्छेद 108"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 106</b><br><b><u>Article 106</u></b> states that members of either House of Parliament shall receive such <b>salaries and allowances</b> as Parliament may determine by law.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 102</b> – disqualifications for membership of Parliament.<br>• <b>Article 104</b> – penalty for sitting and voting when not qualified or disqualified.<br>• <b>Article 108</b> – <b>joint sitting</b> of both Houses, presided over by the Lok Sabha Speaker.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 106</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 106</u></b> के अनुसार संसद के किसी भी सदन के सदस्य ऐसे <b>वेतन और भत्ते</b> प्राप्त करेंगे जो संसद विधि द्वारा निर्धारित करे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 102</b> – संसद की सदस्यता के लिए निरर्हताएँ।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 104</b> – अयोग्य होने पर बैठने और मतदान करने के लिए दंड।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 108</b> – दोनों सदनों की <b>संयुक्त बैठक (Joint sitting)</b>, जिसकी अध्यक्षता लोकसभा अध्यक्ष करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000072210","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Emergency & Constitutional Amendment","question":{"en":"Financial Emergency in India comes under which Article of the Constitution? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत में वित्तीय आपातकाल संविधान के किस अनुच्छेद के अंतर्गत आता है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 352","hi":"अनुच्छेद 352"},"2":{"en":"Article 356","hi":"अनुच्छेद 356"},"3":{"en":"Article 360","hi":"अनुच्छेद 360"},"4":{"en":"Article 368","hi":"अनुच्छेद 368"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 360</b><br><b><u>Article 360</u></b> empowers the President to proclaim a <b>Financial Emergency</b> if the financial stability or credit of India or any part of it is threatened.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Financial Emergency has <b>never been declared</b> in India; it must be approved by Parliament within <b>two months</b>.<br>• <b>Article 352</b> – National Emergency; <b>Article 356</b> – President's Rule in States.<br>• <b>Article 368</b> – power of Parliament to amend the Constitution.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 360</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 360</u></b> राष्ट्रपति को भारत या उसके किसी भाग की वित्तीय स्थिरता या साख खतरे में होने पर <b>वित्तीय आपातकाल</b> घोषित करने का अधिकार देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में वित्तीय आपातकाल <b>कभी घोषित नहीं</b> हुआ; इसे <b>दो माह</b> के भीतर संसद का अनुमोदन आवश्यक है।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 352</b> – राष्ट्रीय आपातकाल; <b>अनुच्छेद 356</b> – राज्यों में राष्ट्रपति शासन।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 368</b> – संविधान संशोधन की संसद की शक्ति।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000072211","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Magnetic Effect of Electric Current","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the SI unit of magnetic flux? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा चुंबकीय फ्लक्स का SI मात्रक है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Farad","hi":"फैराड"},"2":{"en":"Henry","hi":"हेनरी"},"3":{"en":"Pascal","hi":"पास्कल"},"4":{"en":"Weber","hi":"वेबर"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Weber</b><br>The SI unit of <b>magnetic flux</b> is the <b><u>weber (Wb)</u></b>. 1 Wb = 1 tesla × 1 m².<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Farad</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Capacitance</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Henry</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Inductance</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Pascal</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Pressure</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Tesla</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Magnetic field (flux density)</td></tr></table><br>• CGS unit of magnetic flux is the <b>maxwell</b>; 1 Wb = 10<sup>8</sup> maxwell.<br>• Faraday's law: induced emf = rate of change of magnetic flux, \\(e = -\\frac{d\\phi}{dt}\\).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – वेबर</b><br><b>चुंबकीय फ्लक्स (Magnetic flux)</b> का SI मात्रक <b><u>वेबर (Wb)</u></b> है। 1 Wb = 1 टेस्ला × 1 m²।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">फैराड (Farad)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">धारिता (Capacitance)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">हेनरी (Henry)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">प्रेरकत्व (Inductance)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">पास्कल (Pascal)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">दाब (Pressure)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">टेस्ला (Tesla)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">चुंबकीय क्षेत्र (फ्लक्स घनत्व)</td></tr></table><br>• चुंबकीय फ्लक्स का CGS मात्रक <b>मैक्सवेल (Maxwell)</b> है; 1 Wb = 10<sup>8</sup> मैक्सवेल।<br>• फैराडे का नियम: प्रेरित विद्युत वाहक बल = चुंबकीय फ्लक्स में परिवर्तन की दर, \\(e = -\\frac{d\\phi}{dt}\\)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000072212","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"Which ocean contains the point where the Equator intersects the Prime Meridian? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस महासागर में वह बिंदु स्थित है जहाँ भूमध्य रेखा प्रधान याम्योत्तर को काटती है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pacific Ocean","hi":"प्रशांत महासागर"},"2":{"en":"Atlantic Ocean","hi":"अटलांटिक महासागर"},"3":{"en":"Indian Ocean","hi":"हिंद महासागर"},"4":{"en":"Arctic Ocean","hi":"आर्कटिक महासागर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Atlantic Ocean</b><br>The point 0° latitude, 0° longitude lies in the <b><u>Atlantic Ocean</u></b>, in the <b>Gulf of Guinea</b> off the west coast of Africa.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• This point is popularly called <b>\"Null Island\"</b>.<br>• The Prime Meridian passes through <b>Greenwich, London</b>; it was adopted in <b>1884</b>.<br>• The Equator passes through <b>13 countries</b>, including <b>Ecuador, Brazil, Gabon, Kenya and Indonesia</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अटलांटिक महासागर</b><br>0° अक्षांश, 0° देशांतर का बिंदु <b><u>अटलांटिक महासागर</u></b> में, अफ्रीका के पश्चिमी तट के पास <b>गिनी की खाड़ी (Gulf of Guinea)</b> में स्थित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस बिंदु को लोकप्रिय रूप से <b>\"नल आइलैंड (Null Island)\"</b> कहा जाता है।<br>• प्रधान याम्योत्तर <b>ग्रीनविच, लंदन</b> से गुजरता है; इसे <b>1884</b> में अपनाया गया।<br>• भूमध्य रेखा <b>13 देशों</b> से गुजरती है, जिनमें <b>इक्वाडोर, ब्राज़ील, गैबॉन, केन्या और इंडोनेशिया</b> शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000072213","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Cereals cover approximately what percentage of the total cropped area in India? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अनाज भारत के कुल फसल क्षेत्र का लगभग कितना प्रतिशत भाग घेरते हैं? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25%"},"2":{"en":"45%"},"3":{"en":"54%"},"4":{"en":"80%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 54%</b><br>As per NCERT (India – People and Economy), <b>cereals</b> occupy about <b><u>54%</u></b> of the total cropped area of India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Cereals are divided into <b>fine grains</b> (rice, wheat) and <b>coarse grains/millets</b> (jowar, bajra, maize, ragi).<br>• <b>Rice</b> covers about one-fourth of the total cropped area.<br>• India is the <b>second largest producer</b> of rice and wheat after China.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 54%</b><br>NCERT (भारत – लोग और अर्थव्यवस्था) के अनुसार <b>अनाज (Cereals)</b> भारत के कुल फसल क्षेत्र का लगभग <b><u>54%</u></b> भाग घेरते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अनाज को <b>महीन अनाज</b> (चावल, गेहूँ) और <b>मोटे अनाज/मिलेट्स (Coarse grains)</b> (ज्वार, बाजरा, मक्का, रागी) में बाँटा जाता है।<br>• <b>चावल</b> कुल फसल क्षेत्र का लगभग एक-चौथाई भाग घेरता है।<br>• भारत चीन के बाद चावल और गेहूँ का <b>दूसरा सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000072214","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Which of the following best describes the primary ecological function of a food web within a natural habitat? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा प्राकृतिक आवास में खाद्य जाल (food web) के प्राथमिक पारिस्थितिक कार्य का सबसे अच्छा वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It shows a series of branching lines of interconnected food chains","hi":"यह परस्पर जुड़ी खाद्य शृंखलाओं की शाखित रेखाओं की एक शृंखला दर्शाता है"},"2":{"en":"It shows the seasonal migration routes of various animal species in a region","hi":"यह किसी क्षेत्र में विभिन्न जंतु प्रजातियों के मौसमी प्रवास मार्ग दर्शाता है"},"3":{"en":"It estimates the total biomass of producers present at a given trophic level","hi":"यह किसी पोषी स्तर पर उत्पादकों के कुल जैवभार का आकलन करता है"},"4":{"en":"It identifies the dominant predators that control the population sizes of other species","hi":"यह उन प्रमुख शिकारियों की पहचान करता है जो अन्य प्रजातियों की संख्या नियंत्रित करते हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – It shows a series of branching lines of interconnected food chains</b><br>A <b>food web</b> is a network of many <b><u>interconnected food chains</u></b>. It shows the many feeding links in an ecosystem and gives it stability, since organisms have alternative food sources.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Energy flow in an ecosystem is <b>unidirectional</b>; only about <b>10%</b> passes to the next trophic level (<b>Lindeman's 10% law</b>).<br>• Biomass at different trophic levels is shown by an <b>ecological pyramid</b>.<br>• Producers (autotrophs) form the <b>first trophic level</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – यह परस्पर जुड़ी खाद्य शृंखलाओं की शाखित रेखाओं की एक शृंखला दर्शाता है</b><br><b>खाद्य जाल (Food web)</b> कई <b><u>परस्पर जुड़ी खाद्य शृंखलाओं</u></b> का जाल है। यह पारितंत्र में भोजन के अनेक संबंध दिखाता है और उसे स्थिरता देता है, क्योंकि जीवों के पास वैकल्पिक भोजन स्रोत होते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पारितंत्र में ऊर्जा प्रवाह <b>एकदिशीय (Unidirectional)</b> होता है; अगले पोषी स्तर तक केवल लगभग <b>10%</b> ऊर्जा पहुँचती है (<b>लिंडेमैन का 10% नियम</b>)।<br>• विभिन्न पोषी स्तरों का जैवभार <b>पारिस्थितिक पिरामिड (Ecological pyramid)</b> द्वारा दिखाया जाता है।<br>• उत्पादक (स्वपोषी) <b>प्रथम पोषी स्तर</b> बनाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000072215","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Human Eye and Vision","question":{"en":"Excessive curvature of the eye lens causes which defect? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नेत्र लेंस की अत्यधिक वक्रता से कौन-सा दोष होता है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Presbyopia","hi":"जरादूरदृष्टिता"},"2":{"en":"Hypermetropia","hi":"दूरदृष्टि दोष"},"3":{"en":"Myopia","hi":"निकट दृष्टि दोष"},"4":{"en":"Night blindness","hi":"रतौंधी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Myopia</b><br>Excessive curvature of the eye lens (or elongation of the eyeball) brings the image of distant objects in front of the retina. This is <b><u>myopia (near-sightedness)</u></b>, corrected by a <b>concave lens</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Hypermetropia</b> – image forms behind the retina; corrected by a <b>convex lens</b>.<br>• <b>Presbyopia</b> – weakening of ciliary muscles with age; corrected by <b>bifocal lens</b>.<br>• <b>Night blindness</b> is caused by deficiency of <b>Vitamin A</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – निकट दृष्टि दोष</b><br>नेत्र लेंस की अत्यधिक वक्रता (या नेत्रगोलक के लंबा होने) से दूर की वस्तुओं का प्रतिबिंब रेटिना के आगे बनता है। यह <b><u>निकट दृष्टि दोष (Myopia)</u></b> है, जिसे <b>अवतल लेंस (Concave lens)</b> से ठीक किया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>दूरदृष्टि दोष (Hypermetropia)</b> – प्रतिबिंब रेटिना के पीछे बनता है; <b>उत्तल लेंस (Convex lens)</b> से सुधार।<br>• <b>जरादूरदृष्टिता (Presbyopia)</b> – उम्र के साथ पक्ष्माभी पेशियों का कमज़ोर होना; <b>द्विफोकसी लेंस (Bifocal lens)</b> से सुधार।<br>• <b>रतौंधी (Night blindness)</b> <b>विटामिन A</b> की कमी से होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000072216","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Consider the following pairs of legendary musicians and their associated Gharanas:<br>1. Ustad Ali Akbar Khan – Maihar Gharana<br>2. Pandit Bhimsen Joshi – Kirana Gharana<br>Which of the pairs given above is/are <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"महान संगीतकारों और उनसे संबद्ध घरानों के निम्नलिखित युग्मों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. उस्ताद अली अकबर खान – मैहर घराना<br>2. पंडित भीमसेन जोशी – किराना घराना<br>ऊपर दिए गए युग्मों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है/हैं? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br><b>Ustad Ali Akbar Khan</b> (sarod) belonged to the <b>Maihar Gharana</b> founded by his father Baba Allauddin Khan, and <b>Pt. Bhimsen Joshi</b> was a vocalist of the <b>Kirana Gharana</b>. Both pairs are correct: <b><u>Both 1 and 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Bhimsen Joshi</b> received the <b>Bharat Ratna in 2008</b>; his guru was Sawai Gandharva.<br>• <b>Pt. Ravi Shankar</b> (sitar) also belonged to the Maihar Gharana.<br>• Kirana Gharana was founded by <b>Ustad Abdul Karim Khan</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br><b>उस्ताद अली अकबर खान</b> (सरोद) अपने पिता बाबा अलाउद्दीन खान द्वारा स्थापित <b>मैहर घराने</b> से थे और <b>पं. भीमसेन जोशी</b> <b>किराना घराने</b> के गायक थे। दोनों युग्म सही हैं: <b><u>1 और 2 दोनों</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>भीमसेन जोशी</b> को <b>2008 में भारत रत्न</b> मिला; उनके गुरु सवाई गंधर्व थे।<br>• <b>पं. रवि शंकर</b> (सितार) भी मैहर घराने से थे।<br>• किराना घराने की स्थापना <b>उस्ताद अब्दुल करीम खान</b> ने की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000072217","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"What is the main objective of the BHASHINI Mission under the National Language Translation Mission (NLTM)? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"राष्ट्रीय भाषा अनुवाद मिशन (NLTM) के अंतर्गत भाषिणी मिशन का मुख्य उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Teaching Sanskrit in all schools","hi":"सभी विद्यालयों में संस्कृत पढ़ाना"},"2":{"en":"Real-time AI language translation","hi":"रीयल-टाइम AI भाषा अनुवाद"},"3":{"en":"Translating ancient manuscripts","hi":"प्राचीन पांडुलिपियों का अनुवाद"},"4":{"en":"Regulating social media content","hi":"सोशल मीडिया सामग्री का विनियमन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Real-time AI language translation</b><br><b>BHASHINI</b> (BHASHa INterface for India) uses <b>Artificial Intelligence</b> to provide <b><u>real-time translation</u></b> across Indian languages, so that digital services are available in every citizen's own language.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Launched in <b>July 2022</b> by the <b>Ministry of Electronics and IT (MeitY)</b> under Digital India.<br>• Implemented by the <b>Digital India BHASHINI Division</b>.<br>• The Eighth Schedule of the Constitution lists <b>22 languages</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – रीयल-टाइम AI भाषा अनुवाद</b><br><b>भाषिणी (BHASHa INterface for India)</b> <b>कृत्रिम बुद्धिमत्ता (AI)</b> का उपयोग करके भारतीय भाषाओं में <b><u>रीयल-टाइम अनुवाद</u></b> उपलब्ध कराता है, ताकि डिजिटल सेवाएँ हर नागरिक को उसकी अपनी भाषा में मिलें।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>जुलाई 2022</b> में डिजिटल इंडिया के तहत <b>इलेक्ट्रॉनिकी और सूचना प्रौद्योगिकी मंत्रालय (MeitY)</b> द्वारा शुरू।<br>• <b>डिजिटल इंडिया भाषिणी प्रभाग</b> द्वारा कार्यान्वित।<br>• संविधान की आठवीं अनुसूची में <b>22 भाषाएँ</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000072218","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"The emphasis on “South-South Cooperation” within BRICS (Brazil, Russia, India, China, and South Africa) primarily implies cooperation among: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"ब्रिक्स (ब्राज़ील, रूस, भारत, चीन और दक्षिण अफ्रीका) में “दक्षिण-दक्षिण सहयोग” पर ज़ोर मुख्य रूप से किनके बीच सहयोग को दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Developed industrial economies","hi":"विकसित औद्योगिक अर्थव्यवस्थाएँ"},"2":{"en":"Socialist states only","hi":"केवल समाजवादी राज्य"},"3":{"en":"Developing and emerging economies","hi":"विकासशील और उभरती अर्थव्यवस्थाएँ"},"4":{"en":"Northern Hemisphere countries","hi":"उत्तरी गोलार्ध के देश"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Developing and emerging economies</b><br><b>\"Global South\"</b> refers to developing countries, so <b>South-South Cooperation</b> means cooperation among <b><u>developing and emerging economies</u></b> in trade, technology and development finance.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• BRIC was formed in <b>2006</b>; first summit in <b>2009 (Yekaterinburg, Russia)</b>; South Africa joined in <b>2010</b>.<br>• BRICS <b>New Development Bank</b> – HQ <b>Shanghai</b>, set up in 2015.<br>• The term BRIC was coined by <b>Jim O'Neill</b> of Goldman Sachs in 2001.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – विकासशील और उभरती अर्थव्यवस्थाएँ</b><br><b>\"ग्लोबल साउथ\"</b> विकासशील देशों को कहा जाता है, अतः <b>दक्षिण-दक्षिण सहयोग</b> का अर्थ है व्यापार, प्रौद्योगिकी और विकास वित्त में <b><u>विकासशील और उभरती अर्थव्यवस्थाओं</u></b> के बीच सहयोग।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BRIC का गठन <b>2006</b> में; पहला शिखर सम्मेलन <b>2009 (येकातेरिनबर्ग, रूस)</b>; दक्षिण अफ्रीका <b>2010</b> में शामिल हुआ।<br>• ब्रिक्स <b>न्यू डेवलपमेंट बैंक (NDB)</b> – मुख्यालय <b>शंघाई</b>, 2015 में स्थापित।<br>• BRIC शब्द 2001 में गोल्डमैन सैक्स के <b>जिम ओ'नील</b> ने दिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000072219","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"BRICS (Brazil, Russia, India, China, and South Africa) summits are generally characterized by: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"ब्रिक्स (ब्राज़ील, रूस, भारत, चीन और दक्षिण अफ्रीका) शिखर सम्मेलनों की सामान्य विशेषता क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Enforcement sanctions on member states","hi":"सदस्य देशों पर प्रवर्तन प्रतिबंध"},"2":{"en":"Judicial dispute settlement mechanisms","hi":"न्यायिक विवाद निपटान तंत्र"},"3":{"en":"Consensus-based political declarations","hi":"सर्वसम्मति-आधारित राजनीतिक घोषणाएँ"},"4":{"en":"Legally binding treaty negotiations","hi":"कानूनी रूप से बाध्यकारी संधि वार्ताएँ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Consensus-based political declarations</b><br>BRICS is an <b>informal grouping without a charter or secretariat</b>. Its summits end with <b><u>consensus-based declarations</u></b> (e.g., Johannesburg, Kazan, Rio declarations) that are political, not legally binding.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• BRICS chairship rotates in the order <b>B-R-I-C-S</b>; India chairs BRICS in <b>2026</b>.<br>• Expanded members include <b>Egypt, Ethiopia, Iran, UAE</b> (2024) and <b>Indonesia</b> (2025).<br>• <b>Contingent Reserve Arrangement (CRA)</b> provides liquidity support to members.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सर्वसम्मति-आधारित राजनीतिक घोषणाएँ</b><br>ब्रिक्स <b>बिना चार्टर या सचिवालय वाला अनौपचारिक समूह</b> है। इसके शिखर सम्मेलन <b><u>सर्वसम्मति-आधारित घोषणाओं</u></b> (जैसे जोहान्सबर्ग, कज़ान, रियो घोषणाएँ) के साथ समाप्त होते हैं, जो राजनीतिक होती हैं, कानूनी रूप से बाध्यकारी नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ब्रिक्स की अध्यक्षता <b>B-R-I-C-S</b> क्रम में घूमती है; <b>2026</b> में भारत ब्रिक्स का अध्यक्ष है।<br>• विस्तारित सदस्यों में <b>मिस्र, इथियोपिया, ईरान, UAE</b> (2024) और <b>इंडोनेशिया</b> (2025) शामिल हैं।<br>• <b>आकस्मिक रिज़र्व व्यवस्था (CRA)</b> सदस्यों को तरलता सहायता देती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000072220","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A sees B attempting to kidnap C into a vehicle. A shoots B dead to prevent the kidnapping. Which of the following is the strongest legal justification under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"A देखता है कि B, C का अपहरण कर उसे वाहन में ले जाने का प्रयास कर रहा है। A अपहरण रोकने के लिए B को गोली मार देता है। भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के तहत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा सबसे मज़बूत कानूनी औचित्य है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The act would be justified only if B were armed.","hi":"यह कृत्य तभी उचित होगा जब B सशस्त्र हो।"},"2":{"en":"The act exceeds private defence because kidnapping is not punishable by death.","hi":"यह कृत्य निजी प्रतिरक्षा की सीमा पार करता है क्योंकि अपहरण मृत्युदंडनीय नहीं है।"},"3":{"en":"Private defence extends to death in kidnapping assaults.","hi":"अपहरण के हमलों में निजी प्रतिरक्षा का अधिकार मृत्यु कारित करने तक विस्तृत है।"},"4":{"en":"A may only use non-lethal force unless C is actually abducted.","hi":"जब तक C का वास्तव में अपहरण न हो, A केवल गैर-घातक बल का प्रयोग कर सकता है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Private defence extends to death in kidnapping assaults.</b><br>Under <b>Section 38 of the BNS, 2023</b> (old IPC Sec. 100), the right of private defence of the body <b><u>extends to causing death</u></b> against an assault made with the intention of <b>kidnapping or abducting</b>. The right also protects another person (C).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Private defence is covered in <b>Sections 34–44 of BNS</b> (IPC Secs. 96–106).<br>• Other cases where death may be caused: fear of death or grievous hurt, rape, unnatural lust, acid attack, wrongful confinement with no access to authorities.<br>• BNS replaced the <b>IPC, 1860</b> and came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अपहरण के हमलों में निजी प्रतिरक्षा का अधिकार मृत्यु कारित करने तक विस्तृत है।</b><br><b>BNS, 2023 की धारा 38</b> (पुरानी IPC धारा 100) के तहत शरीर की निजी प्रतिरक्षा का अधिकार <b>व्यपहरण या अपहरण (Kidnapping or abducting)</b> के आशय से किए गए हमले के विरुद्ध <b><u>मृत्यु कारित करने तक विस्तृत</u></b> है। यह अधिकार किसी अन्य व्यक्ति (C) की रक्षा पर भी लागू होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• निजी प्रतिरक्षा <b>BNS की धारा 34–44</b> (IPC धारा 96–106) में है।<br>• अन्य स्थितियाँ जहाँ मृत्यु कारित की जा सकती है: मृत्यु या घोर उपहति का भय, बलात्संग, अप्राकृतिक काम-वासना, तेज़ाब हमला, प्राधिकारियों तक पहुँच न होने पर सदोष परिरोध।<br>• BNS ने <b>IPC, 1860</b> का स्थान लिया और <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से लागू हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000072221","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who has been appointed as the 27<sup>th</sup> Chief of the Naval Staff (CNS) of the Indian Navy in May 2026? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मई 2026 में भारतीय नौसेना के 27वें नौसेना प्रमुख (CNS) के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Admiral Dinesh Kumar Tripathi","hi":"एडमिरल दिनेश कुमार त्रिपाठी"},"2":{"en":"Admiral Krishna Swaminathan","hi":"एडमिरल कृष्णा स्वामीनाथन"},"3":{"en":"Admiral Radhakrishnan Hari Kumar","hi":"एडमिरल राधाकृष्णन हरि कुमार"},"4":{"en":"Vice Admiral Sanjay Vatsayan","hi":"वाइस एडमिरल संजय वत्सायन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Admiral Krishna Swaminathan</b><br><b><u>Admiral Krishna Swaminathan</u></b> took charge as the <b>27<sup>th</sup> Chief of the Naval Staff</b> on <b>31 May 2026</b>, succeeding Admiral Dinesh Kumar Tripathi.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Admiral Dinesh Kumar Tripathi</b> was the 26<sup>th</sup> CNS (April 2024 – May 2026).<br>• <b>Admiral R. Hari Kumar</b> was the 25<sup>th</sup> CNS (2021–2024).<br>• The <b>President of India</b> is the Supreme Commander of the Armed Forces; Navy Day is observed on <b>4 December</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – एडमिरल कृष्णा स्वामीनाथन</b><br><b><u>एडमिरल कृष्णा स्वामीनाथन</u></b> ने <b>31 मई 2026</b> को एडमिरल दिनेश कुमार त्रिपाठी के बाद <b>27वें नौसेना प्रमुख</b> के रूप में कार्यभार संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>एडमिरल दिनेश कुमार त्रिपाठी</b> 26वें नौसेना प्रमुख थे (अप्रैल 2024 – मई 2026)।<br>• <b>एडमिरल आर. हरि कुमार</b> 25वें नौसेना प्रमुख थे (2021–2024)।<br>• <b>भारत के राष्ट्रपति</b> सशस्त्र बलों के सर्वोच्च कमांडर हैं; नौसेना दिवस <b>4 दिसंबर</b> को मनाया जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000072222","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian tennis player, at age 43, set the Open Era record by winning the Australian Open 2024 men’s doubles title? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस भारतीय टेनिस खिलाड़ी ने 43 वर्ष की आयु में ऑस्ट्रेलियन ओपन 2024 पुरुष युगल खिताब जीतकर ओपन युग का रिकॉर्ड बनाया? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Leander Paes","hi":"लिएंडर पेस"},"2":{"en":"Mahesh Bhupathi","hi":"महेश भूपति"},"3":{"en":"Rohan Bopanna","hi":"रोहन बोपन्ना"},"4":{"en":"Sumit Nagal","hi":"सुमित नागल"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Rohan Bopanna</b><br><b><u>Rohan Bopanna</u></b>, partnering <b>Matthew Ebden</b> (Australia), won the 2024 Australian Open men's doubles and became the <b>oldest man in the Open Era</b> to win a Grand Slam title.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In the same year Bopanna became the <b>oldest World No. 1</b> in men's doubles.<br>• Australian Open is played on <b>hard courts</b> in <b>Melbourne</b>; it is the first Grand Slam of the year.<br>• Bopanna's earlier Grand Slam: <b>2017 French Open mixed doubles</b> (with Gabriela Dabrowski).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – रोहन बोपन्ना</b><br><b><u>रोहन बोपन्ना</u></b> ने <b>मैथ्यू एबडेन</b> (ऑस्ट्रेलिया) के साथ 2024 ऑस्ट्रेलियन ओपन पुरुष युगल जीता और ओपन युग में ग्रैंड स्लैम खिताब जीतने वाले <b>सबसे उम्रदराज़ पुरुष</b> बने।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उसी वर्ष बोपन्ना पुरुष युगल में <b>सबसे उम्रदराज़ विश्व नंबर 1</b> बने।<br>• ऑस्ट्रेलियन ओपन <b>मेलबर्न</b> में <b>हार्ड कोर्ट</b> पर खेला जाता है; यह वर्ष का पहला ग्रैंड स्लैम है।<br>• बोपन्ना का पूर्व ग्रैंड स्लैम: <b>2017 फ्रेंच ओपन मिश्रित युगल</b> (गैब्रिएला डाब्रोवस्की के साथ)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000072223","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: State News","question":{"en":"In June 2026, which of the following protected areas in Assam recorded its first-ever sighting of the Yellow-throated Marten? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जून 2026 में असम के निम्नलिखित संरक्षित क्षेत्रों में से किसमें पीले गले वाले मार्टन (Yellow-throated Marten) को पहली बार देखा गया? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Manas National Park","hi":"मानस राष्ट्रीय उद्यान"},"2":{"en":"Nameri National Park","hi":"नामेरी राष्ट्रीय उद्यान"},"3":{"en":"Kaziranga National Park","hi":"काज़ीरंगा राष्ट्रीय उद्यान"},"4":{"en":"Dibru-Saikhowa National Park","hi":"डिब्रू-सैखोवा राष्ट्रीय उद्यान"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Kaziranga National Park</b><br>In early June 2026, <b><u>Kaziranga National Park</u></b> recorded the <b>Yellow-throated Marten</b> for the first time, adding a new mammal species to the park's records.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Yellow-throated Marten is a member of the <b>Mustelidae (weasel) family</b>; listed as <b>Least Concern</b> on the IUCN Red List.<br>• Kaziranga is a <b>UNESCO World Heritage Site (1985)</b>, famous for the <b>one-horned rhinoceros</b>; declared a Tiger Reserve in <b>2006</b>.<br>• <b>Manas</b> is also a UNESCO World Heritage Site; <b>Dibru-Saikhowa</b> is known for feral horses.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – काज़ीरंगा राष्ट्रीय उद्यान</b><br>जून 2026 की शुरुआत में <b><u>काज़ीरंगा राष्ट्रीय उद्यान</u></b> में पहली बार <b>पीले गले वाला मार्टन (Yellow-throated Marten)</b> दर्ज किया गया, जिससे उद्यान की सूची में एक नई स्तनधारी प्रजाति जुड़ी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पीले गले वाला मार्टन <b>मस्टेलिडी (नेवला) कुल</b> का सदस्य है; IUCN रेड लिस्ट में <b>संकटमुक्त (Least Concern)</b>।<br>• काज़ीरंगा <b>यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल (1985)</b> है, <b>एक सींग वाले गैंडे</b> के लिए प्रसिद्ध; <b>2006</b> में बाघ अभयारण्य घोषित।<br>• <b>मानस</b> भी यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल है; <b>डिब्रू-सैखोवा</b> जंगली घोड़ों के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000072224","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which ISRO launch vehicle is being upgraded with the Semicryogenic Engine (SE2000)? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"इसरो के किस प्रक्षेपण यान को सेमीक्रायोजेनिक इंजन (SE2000) से उन्नत किया जा रहा है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle (PSLV)","hi":"ध्रुवीय उपग्रह प्रक्षेपण यान (PSLV)"},"2":{"en":"Geosynchronous Satellite Launch Vehicle (GSLV Mk II)","hi":"भूतुल्यकाली उपग्रह प्रक्षेपण यान (GSLV Mk II)"},"3":{"en":"Launch Vehicle Mark-3 (LVM3)","hi":"लॉन्च व्हीकल मार्क-3 (LVM3)"},"4":{"en":"Small Satellite Launch Vehicle (SSLV)","hi":"लघु उपग्रह प्रक्षेपण यान (SSLV)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Launch Vehicle Mark-3 (LVM3)</b><br>The <b>SE2000</b> semicryogenic engine (LOX + kerosene, about 2000 kN thrust) will power a new <b>SC120 stage</b> that replaces the L110 core stage of <b><u>LVM3</u></b>, raising its GTO payload capacity.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The engine is developed by ISRO's <b>Liquid Propulsion Systems Centre (LPSC)</b>.<br>• LVM3 launched <b>Chandrayaan-2, Chandrayaan-3</b> and is the vehicle for <b>Gaganyaan</b> (HLVM3).<br>• <b>PSLV</b> – workhorse with 4 stages; <b>SSLV</b> – for satellites up to 500 kg in LEO.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – लॉन्च व्हीकल मार्क-3 (LVM3)</b><br><b>SE2000</b> सेमीक्रायोजेनिक इंजन (द्रव ऑक्सीजन + केरोसीन, लगभग 2000 kN प्रणोद) एक नए <b>SC120 चरण</b> को शक्ति देगा, जो <b><u>LVM3</u></b> के L110 कोर चरण का स्थान लेगा और इसकी GTO पेलोड क्षमता बढ़ाएगा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह इंजन इसरो के <b>द्रव नोदन प्रणाली केंद्र (LPSC)</b> द्वारा विकसित है।<br>• LVM3 ने <b>चंद्रयान-2, चंद्रयान-3</b> प्रक्षेपित किए और यही <b>गगनयान</b> (HLVM3) का यान है।<br>• <b>PSLV</b> – 4 चरणों वाला वर्कहॉर्स; <b>SSLV</b> – LEO में 500 kg तक के उपग्रहों के लिए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000072225","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: National Income","question":{"en":"Which of the following statement regarding Net Domestic Product (NDP) at market prices is <b>correct</b>? (GDP =Gross Domestic Product) [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बाज़ार मूल्य पर निवल घरेलू उत्पाद (NDP) के संबंध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन <b>सही</b> है? (GDP = सकल घरेलू उत्पाद) [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Net Domestic Product at market prices exceeds GDP at market prices by the amount of depreciation.","hi":"बाज़ार मूल्य पर निवल घरेलू उत्पाद, बाज़ार मूल्य पर GDP से मूल्यह्रास की राशि जितना अधिक होता है।"},"2":{"en":"Net Domestic Product at market prices equals GDP at market prices after deducting depreciation.","hi":"बाज़ार मूल्य पर निवल घरेलू उत्पाद, मूल्यह्रास घटाने के बाद बाज़ार मूल्य पर GDP के बराबर होता है।"},"3":{"en":"Net Domestic Product at market prices equals GDP at market prices after adding indirect taxes.","hi":"बाज़ार मूल्य पर निवल घरेलू उत्पाद, अप्रत्यक्ष कर जोड़ने के बाद बाज़ार मूल्य पर GDP के बराबर होता है।"},"4":{"en":"Net Domestic Product at market prices excludes both depreciation and net factor income abroad.","hi":"बाज़ार मूल्य पर निवल घरेलू उत्पाद में मूल्यह्रास और विदेश से निवल साधन आय दोनों शामिल नहीं होते।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Net Domestic Product at market prices equals GDP at market prices after deducting depreciation.</b><br>\\(\\text{NDP}_{MP} = \\text{GDP}_{MP} - \\text{Depreciation}\\)<br>So NDP at market prices equals <b><u>GDP at market prices minus depreciation</u></b> (consumption of fixed capital).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• \\(\\text{GNP} = \\text{GDP} + \\text{NFIA}\\) (Net Factor Income from Abroad).<br>• \\(\\text{Factor Cost} = \\text{Market Price} - \\text{Net Indirect Taxes}\\) (Indirect taxes − Subsidies).<br>• <b>NNP at factor cost</b> is called <b>National Income</b>; in India it is estimated by the <b>NSO (MoSPI)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बाज़ार मूल्य पर निवल घरेलू उत्पाद, मूल्यह्रास घटाने के बाद बाज़ार मूल्य पर GDP के बराबर होता है।</b><br>\\(\\text{NDP}_{MP} = \\text{GDP}_{MP} - \\text{Depreciation}\\)<br>अतः बाज़ार मूल्य पर NDP = <b><u>बाज़ार मूल्य पर GDP – मूल्यह्रास (Depreciation)</u></b> (स्थिर पूँजी का उपभोग)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• \\(\\text{GNP} = \\text{GDP} + \\text{NFIA}\\) (विदेश से निवल साधन आय – Net Factor Income from Abroad)।<br>• \\(\\text{Factor Cost} = \\text{Market Price} - \\text{Net Indirect Taxes}\\) (अप्रत्यक्ष कर − सब्सिडी)।<br>• <b>साधन लागत पर NNP</b> को <b>राष्ट्रीय आय (National Income)</b> कहते हैं; भारत में इसका आकलन <b>NSO (MoSPI)</b> करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000072226","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"During the 1991 economic crisis, India's foreign exchange reserves dropped to a level that was sufficient to finance imports for only how long? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक संकट के दौरान भारत का विदेशी मुद्रा भंडार उस स्तर तक गिर गया था जो केवल कितने समय के आयात के लिए पर्याप्त था? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"One month","hi":"एक महीना"},"2":{"en":"Two weeks","hi":"दो सप्ताह"},"3":{"en":"One week","hi":"एक सप्ताह"},"4":{"en":"Three months","hi":"तीन महीने"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Two weeks</b><br>In mid-1991, India's foreign exchange reserves fell to about <b>1.1 billion US dollars</b>, enough to pay for imports of only about <b><u>two weeks</u></b>, triggering a severe balance of payments crisis.<br><br><br><b><u>Causes of the Crisis:</u></b><br>• Large <b>fiscal deficit</b> and <b>balance of payments deficit</b> during the 1980s.<br>• Rise in oil prices due to the <b>Gulf War (1990-91)</b> and a fall in remittances from the Gulf region.<br>• Heavy dependence on <b>short-term external borrowing</b> and political instability.<br><br><b><u>Steps Taken to Raise Funds:</u></b><br>• <b>May 1991:</b> About <b>20 tonnes of gold</b> was pledged to the <b>Union Bank of Switzerland (UBS)</b>, raising about 200 million US dollars.<br>• <b>July 1991:</b> About <b>47 tonnes of gold</b> was pledged to the <b>Bank of England and Bank of Japan</b>, raising about 400 million US dollars.<br>• <b>IMF loan:</b> India took a loan from the <b>IMF</b> (about 2.2 billion US dollars) under <b>structural adjustment conditions</b>.<br><br><b><u>Reforms Introduced (LPG):</u></b><br>• <b>1 and 3 July 1991:</b> The rupee was <b>devalued</b> in two steps (about 18-19% in total).<br>• <b>24 July 1991:</b> The <b>New Industrial Policy</b> was announced, which ended <b>industrial licensing</b> for most industries, eased MRTP limits, and allowed greater <b>foreign investment</b>.<br>• The reforms were led by PM <b>P. V. Narasimha Rao</b> and Finance Minister <b>Dr. Manmohan Singh</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – दो सप्ताह</b><br>1991 के मध्य में भारत का विदेशी मुद्रा भंडार लगभग <b>1.1 अरब अमेरिकी डॉलर</b> रह गया, जो केवल लगभग <b><u>दो सप्ताह</u></b> के आयात के लिए पर्याप्त था, जिससे गंभीर भुगतान संतुलन संकट उत्पन्न हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>संकट के कारण:</u></b><br>• 1980 के दशक में बड़ा <b>राजकोषीय घाटा</b> और <b>भुगतान संतुलन घाटा</b>।<br>• <b>खाड़ी युद्ध (1990-91)</b> के कारण तेल की कीमतों में वृद्धि और खाड़ी देशों से आने वाले धन (रेमिटेंस) में गिरावट।<br>• <b>अल्पकालिक विदेशी ऋणों</b> पर अत्यधिक निर्भरता और राजनीतिक अस्थिरता।<br><br><b><u>धन जुटाने के लिए उठाए गए कदम:</u></b><br>• <b>मई 1991:</b> लगभग <b>20 टन सोना</b> <b>यूनियन बैंक ऑफ स्विट्जरलैंड (UBS)</b> के पास गिरवी रखा गया, जिससे लगभग 20 करोड़ अमेरिकी डॉलर जुटाए गए।<br>• <b>जुलाई 1991:</b> लगभग <b>47 टन सोना</b> <b>बैंक ऑफ इंग्लैंड और बैंक ऑफ जापान</b> के पास गिरवी रखा गया, जिससे लगभग 40 करोड़ अमेरिकी डॉलर जुटाए गए।<br>• <b>IMF ऋण:</b> भारत ने <b>संरचनात्मक समायोजन शर्तों</b> के साथ <b>IMF</b> से लगभग 2.2 अरब अमेरिकी डॉलर का ऋण लिया।<br><br><b><u>लागू किए गए सुधार (LPG):</u></b><br>• <b>1 और 3 जुलाई 1991:</b> रुपये का दो चरणों में <b>अवमूल्यन</b> किया गया (कुल लगभग 18-19%)।<br>• <b>24 जुलाई 1991:</b> <b>नई औद्योगिक नीति</b> घोषित हुई, जिसमें अधिकांश उद्योगों के लिए <b>औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग</b> समाप्त की गई, MRTP सीमाएँ ढीली की गईं और <b>विदेशी निवेश</b> को बढ़ावा मिला।<br>• ये सुधार प्रधानमंत्री <b>पी. वी. नरसिम्हा राव</b> और वित्त मंत्री <b>डॉ. मनमोहन सिंह</b> के नेतृत्व में हुए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000072227","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Human Geography","question":{"en":"Which technology is primarily emphasized in the URDPFI (Urban and Regional Development Plans Formulation and Implementation) Guidelines for improving the speed and efficiency of urban planning and spatial analysis? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"शहरी नियोजन और स्थानिक विश्लेषण की गति और दक्षता सुधारने के लिए URDPFI (शहरी और क्षेत्रीय विकास योजना निर्माण और कार्यान्वयन) दिशानिर्देशों में मुख्य रूप से किस प्रौद्योगिकी पर ज़ोर दिया गया है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Remote Sensing and GIS (Geographic Information System)","hi":"सुदूर संवेदन और GIS (भौगोलिक सूचना प्रणाली)"},"2":{"en":"Blockchain","hi":"ब्लॉकचेन"},"3":{"en":"Robotics","hi":"रोबोटिक्स"},"4":{"en":"IoT (Internet of Things)","hi":"IoT (इंटरनेट ऑफ थिंग्स)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Remote Sensing and GIS (Geographic Information System)</b><br>The URDPFI Guidelines recommend <b><u>Remote Sensing and GIS</u></b> for preparing base maps, land-use surveys and spatial analysis, which makes plan preparation faster and more accurate.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• URDPFI Guidelines were issued in <b>2014</b> by the <b>Ministry of Urban Development</b> (now <b>Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs</b>).<br>• They were prepared by <b>Town and Country Planning Organisation (TCPO)</b>.<br>• GIS-based master plans are also a reform under <b>AMRUT</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – सुदूर संवेदन और GIS (भौगोलिक सूचना प्रणाली)</b><br>URDPFI दिशानिर्देश आधार मानचित्र, भूमि-उपयोग सर्वेक्षण और स्थानिक विश्लेषण के लिए <b><u>सुदूर संवेदन (Remote Sensing) और GIS</u></b> के उपयोग की सिफारिश करते हैं, जिससे योजना निर्माण तेज़ और अधिक सटीक होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• URDPFI दिशानिर्देश <b>2014</b> में <b>शहरी विकास मंत्रालय</b> (अब <b>आवास और शहरी कार्य मंत्रालय</b>) द्वारा जारी किए गए।<br>• इन्हें <b>नगर और ग्राम नियोजन संगठन (TCPO)</b> ने तैयार किया।<br>• GIS-आधारित मास्टर प्लान <b>अमृत (AMRUT)</b> के अंतर्गत भी एक सुधार है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000072228","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"Which of the following policy shifts characterized the Tenth Five-Year Plan (2002–2007) in terms of target setting? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"लक्ष्य निर्धारण के संदर्भ में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा नीतिगत बदलाव दसवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (2002–2007) की विशेषता था? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Phasing out centrally sponsored schemes","hi":"केंद्र प्रायोजित योजनाओं को चरणबद्ध तरीके से समाप्त करना"},"2":{"en":"Introducing eleven core monitorable targets","hi":"ग्यारह प्रमुख निगरानी योग्य लक्ष्यों की शुरुआत"},"3":{"en":"Restricting foreign direct investment","hi":"प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश पर प्रतिबंध"},"4":{"en":"Eliminating fiscal deficit targets entirely","hi":"राजकोषीय घाटे के लक्ष्यों को पूरी तरह समाप्त करना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Introducing eleven core monitorable targets</b><br>The Tenth Plan was the first to set <b><u>monitorable targets for 11 key indicators</u></b> of development (poverty, literacy, IMR, MMR, forest cover, employment, etc.) along with a <b>GDP growth target of 8%</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Tenth Plan also set <b>state-wise targets</b> for growth for the first time.<br>• Actual growth achieved was about <b>7.6%</b>.<br>• <b>Eleventh Plan (2007–12)</b> theme: \"Faster and More Inclusive Growth\"; Planning Commission was replaced by <b>NITI Aayog</b> on 1 January 2015.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ग्यारह प्रमुख निगरानी योग्य लक्ष्यों की शुरुआत</b><br>दसवीं योजना पहली योजना थी जिसने विकास के <b><u>11 प्रमुख संकेतकों के लिए निगरानी योग्य लक्ष्य</u></b> (गरीबी, साक्षरता, IMR, MMR, वन आवरण, रोज़गार आदि) तथा <b>8% GDP वृद्धि लक्ष्य</b> निर्धारित किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दसवीं योजना ने पहली बार <b>राज्यवार वृद्धि लक्ष्य</b> भी तय किए।<br>• वास्तविक वृद्धि लगभग <b>7.6%</b> रही।<br>• <b>ग्यारहवीं योजना (2007–12)</b> का विषय: \"तीव्र और अधिक समावेशी विकास\"; 1 जनवरी 2015 को योजना आयोग का स्थान <b>नीति आयोग</b> ने लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000072229","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Making of Constitution","question":{"en":"Under the Indian Independence Act, full legislative authority in each Dominion was vested in which body? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय स्वतंत्रता अधिनियम के तहत प्रत्येक डोमिनियन में पूर्ण विधायी प्राधिकार किस निकाय में निहित किया गया? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"British Parliament","hi":"ब्रिटिश संसद"},"2":{"en":"Governor General","hi":"गवर्नर जनरल"},"3":{"en":"Constituent Assembly","hi":"संविधान सभा"},"4":{"en":"Secretary of State","hi":"भारत सचिव"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Constituent Assembly</b><br>The <b>Indian Independence Act, 1947</b> made the <b><u>Constituent Assembly</u></b> of each Dominion a fully sovereign body, which also acted as the <b>Dominion Legislature</b> until a new constitution came into force.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Act was based on the <b>Mountbatten Plan (3 June 1947)</b> and received royal assent on <b>18 July 1947</b>.<br>• It abolished the office of the <b>Secretary of State for India</b>.<br>• As legislature, the Constituent Assembly was chaired by <b>G.V. Mavalankar</b>; as constitution-making body, by <b>Dr. Rajendra Prasad</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – संविधान सभा</b><br><b>भारतीय स्वतंत्रता अधिनियम, 1947</b> ने प्रत्येक डोमिनियन की <b><u>संविधान सभा</u></b> को पूर्ण संप्रभु निकाय बनाया, जो नए संविधान के लागू होने तक <b>डोमिनियन विधायिका</b> के रूप में भी कार्य करती रही।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह अधिनियम <b>माउंटबेटन योजना (3 जून 1947)</b> पर आधारित था और इसे <b>18 जुलाई 1947</b> को शाही स्वीकृति मिली।<br>• इसने <b>भारत सचिव (Secretary of State)</b> का पद समाप्त कर दिया।<br>• विधायिका के रूप में संविधान सभा की अध्यक्षता <b>जी.वी. मावलंकर</b> ने और संविधान-निर्माण निकाय के रूप में <b>डॉ. राजेंद्र प्रसाद</b> ने की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000072230","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Governor-General and Viceroy","question":{"en":"Which Governor-General of India abolished the practice of sati through Regulation XVII? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत के किस गवर्नर-जनरल ने विनियमन XVII के माध्यम से सती प्रथा को समाप्त किया? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lord Ripon","hi":"लॉर्ड रिपन"},"2":{"en":"Lord William Bentinck","hi":"लॉर्ड विलियम बेंटिक"},"3":{"en":"Lord Dalhousie","hi":"लॉर्ड डलहौज़ी"},"4":{"en":"Lord Cornwallis","hi":"लॉर्ड कॉर्नवालिस"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Lord William Bentinck</b><br><b><u>Lord William Bentinck</u></b> declared sati illegal through the <b>Bengal Sati Regulation XVII of 1829</b> (4 December 1829), supported by <b>Raja Ram Mohan Roy</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bentinck was the <b>first Governor-General of India</b> under the <b>Charter Act of 1833</b>.<br>• <b>Lord Ripon</b> – Father of Local Self-Government (1882); <b>Lord Cornwallis</b> – Permanent Settlement (1793).<br>• <b>Lord Dalhousie</b> – Doctrine of Lapse; Widow Remarriage Act passed in 1856 under Lord Canning.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – लॉर्ड विलियम बेंटिक</b><br><b><u>लॉर्ड विलियम बेंटिक</u></b> ने <b>1829 के बंगाल सती विनियमन XVII</b> (4 दिसंबर 1829) द्वारा सती को अवैध घोषित किया, जिसमें <b>राजा राममोहन राय</b> का समर्थन था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बेंटिक <b>1833 के चार्टर अधिनियम</b> के तहत <b>भारत के पहले गवर्नर-जनरल</b> बने।<br>• <b>लॉर्ड रिपन</b> – स्थानीय स्वशासन के जनक (1882); <b>लॉर्ड कॉर्नवालिस</b> – स्थायी बंदोबस्त (1793)।<br>• <b>लॉर्ड डलहौज़ी</b> – व्यपगत का सिद्धांत (Doctrine of Lapse); विधवा पुनर्विवाह अधिनियम 1856 में लॉर्ड कैनिंग के समय पारित हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000072231","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify: [(1.25 × 1.25 × 1.25 − 1) ÷ (1.25 × 1.25 + 1.25 + 1)] + 0.75. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सरलीकृत कीजिए: [(1.25 × 1.25 × 1.25 − 1) ÷ (1.25 × 1.25 + 1.25 + 1)] + 0.75 [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\) with \\(a = 1.25, b = 1\\)<br>\\(= 1.25 - 1 = 0.25\\)<br>\\(0.25 + 0.75 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\), जहाँ \\(a = 1.25, b = 1\\)<br>\\(= 1.25 - 1 = 0.25\\)<br>\\(0.25 + 0.75 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000072232","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{x}{49}} = \\frac{8}{7}\\), find the value of x. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{x}{49}} = \\frac{8}{7}\\) है, तो x का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"13"},"3":{"en":"15"},"4":{"en":"18"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Squaring both sides: \\(1 + \\frac{x}{49} = \\frac{64}{49}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x}{49} = \\frac{64}{49} - 1 = \\frac{15}{49}\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{15}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 15.</b>","hi":"दोनों पक्षों का वर्ग करने पर: \\(1 + \\frac{x}{49} = \\frac{64}{49}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x}{49} = \\frac{64}{49} - 1 = \\frac{15}{49}\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{15}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000072233","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"Working alone, Pipe P can fill 15% of a tank in 4 hours, and Pipe Q can fill 18% of the same tank in 4 hours. If both pipes are opened together, what percentage of the tank will be filled in 4 hours? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अकेले कार्य करते हुए, पाइप P एक टंकी का 15% भाग 4 घंटे में भर सकता है और पाइप Q उसी टंकी का 18% भाग 4 घंटे में भर सकता है। यदि दोनों पाइप एक साथ खोले जाएँ, तो 4 घंटे में टंकी का कितना प्रतिशत भर जाएगा? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25%"},"2":{"en":"33%"},"3":{"en":"42%"},"4":{"en":"56%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In 4 hours P fills 15% and Q fills 18%<br>Together in 4 hours \\(= 15\\% + 18\\% = 33\\%\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{33\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 33%.</b>","hi":"4 घंटे में P, 15% और Q, 18% भरता है<br>दोनों मिलकर 4 घंटे में \\(= 15\\% + 18\\% = 33\\%\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{33\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 33% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000072234","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"When x is subtracted from each of 20, 28, 25, and 35, the numbers so obtained are in proportion. Find the mean proportional between (x + 2) and (3x + 1). [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जब 20, 28, 25 और 35 में से प्रत्येक से x घटाया जाता है, तो प्राप्त संख्याएँ समानुपात में होती हैं। (x + 2) और (3x + 1) के बीच माध्य समानुपाती ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(3\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((20 - x)(35 - x) = (28 - x)(25 - x)\\)<br>\\(700 - 55x + x^2 = 700 - 53x + x^2 \\Rightarrow 2x = 0 \\Rightarrow x = 0\\)<br>Mean proportional of \\(2\\) and \\(1\\) is \\(\\sqrt{2 \\times 1}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\sqrt{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\((20 - x)(35 - x) = (28 - x)(25 - x)\\)<br>\\(700 - 55x + x^2 = 700 - 53x + x^2 \\Rightarrow 2x = 0 \\Rightarrow x = 0\\)<br>\\(2\\) और \\(1\\) का माध्य समानुपाती \\(\\sqrt{2 \\times 1}\\) है<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\sqrt{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000072235","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A man invests ₹4,000 for 3 years at a certain rate of simple interest. If the principal is increased by ₹2,000 and the rate is kept the same, the interest increases by ₹360. What was the original rate of interest? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति ₹4,000 को 3 वर्षों के लिए किसी साधारण ब्याज दर पर निवेश करता है। यदि मूलधन ₹2,000 बढ़ा दिया जाए और दर वही रहे, तो ब्याज ₹360 बढ़ जाता है। मूल ब्याज दर क्या थी? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5%"},"2":{"en":"8%"},"3":{"en":"6%"},"4":{"en":"10%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Extra principal ₹\\(= 2{,}000\\) for 3 years gives ₹\\(360\\)<br>\\(\\frac{2000 \\times R \\times 3}{100} = 360\\)<br>\\(60R = 360 \\Rightarrow R = \\boxed{6\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 6%.</b>","hi":"अतिरिक्त मूलधन ₹\\(= 2{,}000\\) पर 3 वर्षों का ब्याज ₹\\(360\\) है<br>\\(\\frac{2000 \\times R \\times 3}{100} = 360\\)<br>\\(60R = 360 \\Rightarrow R = \\boxed{6\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 6% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000072236","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x\\left(7 - \\frac{3}{x}\\right) = \\frac{7}{x}\\), then find the value of \\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\). [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(x\\left(7 - \\frac{3}{x}\\right) = \\frac{7}{x}\\) है, तो \\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{107}{49}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{53}{49}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{125}{49}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{47}{49}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(7x - 3 = \\frac{7}{x} \\Rightarrow 7x - \\frac{7}{x} = 3 \\Rightarrow x - \\frac{1}{x} = \\frac{3}{7}\\)<br>\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = \\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 + 2 = \\frac{9}{49} + 2\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{9 + 98}{49} = \\boxed{\\frac{107}{49}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{107}{49}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(7x - 3 = \\frac{7}{x} \\Rightarrow 7x - \\frac{7}{x} = 3 \\Rightarrow x - \\frac{1}{x} = \\frac{3}{7}\\)<br>\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = \\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 + 2 = \\frac{9}{49} + 2\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{9 + 98}{49} = \\boxed{\\frac{107}{49}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{107}{49}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000072237","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"Which type of line has a slope equal to zero? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस प्रकार की रेखा का ढाल शून्य के बराबर होता है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Vertical line","hi":"ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखा"},"2":{"en":"Line making 45° with x-axis","hi":"x-अक्ष से 45° बनाने वाली रेखा"},"3":{"en":"Horizontal line","hi":"क्षैतिज रेखा"},"4":{"en":"Oblique line","hi":"तिर्यक रेखा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Slope \\(= \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}\\)<br>For a horizontal line \\(y_2 = y_1\\), so the slope \\(= 0\\)<br>Hence a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Horizontal line}}\\) has zero slope<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Horizontal line.</b>","hi":"ढाल \\(= \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}\\)<br>क्षैतिज रेखा के लिए \\(y_2 = y_1\\), अतः ढाल \\(= 0\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{\\text{क्षैतिज रेखा}}\\) का ढाल शून्य होता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): क्षैतिज रेखा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000072238","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"₹2,50,000 is invested at 8% compound interest. After 1 year, ₹40,000 is withdrawn. Find the amount after 2 years. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"₹2,50,000 को 8% चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर निवेश किया जाता है। 1 वर्ष बाद ₹40,000 निकाल लिए जाते हैं। 2 वर्ष बाद की राशि ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹2,98,400"},"2":{"en":"₹2,78,400"},"3":{"en":"₹2,48,400"},"4":{"en":"₹2,08,400"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Amount after 1 year \\(= 2{,}50{,}000 \\times 1.08 = 2{,}70{,}000\\)<br>After withdrawal the principal \\(= 2{,}70{,}000 - 40{,}000 = 2{,}30{,}000\\)<br>Amount after 2 years ₹\\(= 2{,}30{,}000 \\times 1.08 = \\boxed{2{,}48{,}400}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹2,48,400.</b>","hi":"1 वर्ष बाद राशि \\(= 2{,}50{,}000 \\times 1.08 = 2{,}70{,}000\\)<br>निकासी के बाद मूलधन \\(= 2{,}70{,}000 - 40{,}000 = 2{,}30{,}000\\)<br>2 वर्ष बाद राशि ₹\\(= 2{,}30{,}000 \\times 1.08 = \\boxed{2{,}48{,}400}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹2,48,400 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000072239","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A rectangular box has dimensions 150 cm × 60 cm × 30 cm. Small cubes of side 5 cm are packed inside without leaving space. How many cubes can be packed? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक आयताकार बक्से की विमाएँ 150 cm × 60 cm × 30 cm हैं। 5 cm भुजा वाले छोटे घन बिना स्थान छोड़े भीतर रखे जाते हैं। कितने घन रखे जा सकते हैं? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2160"},"2":{"en":"2250"},"3":{"en":"1730"},"4":{"en":"1400"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Number of cubes \\(= \\frac{150}{5} \\times \\frac{60}{5} \\times \\frac{30}{5}\\)<br>\\(= 30 \\times 12 \\times 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2160}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2160.</b>","hi":"घनों की संख्या \\(= \\frac{150}{5} \\times \\frac{60}{5} \\times \\frac{30}{5}\\)<br>\\(= 30 \\times 12 \\times 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2160}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2160 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000072240","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord of a circle subtends an angle of 60° at the center. If the radius of the circle is 10 cm, find the length of the chord. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वृत्त की जीवा केंद्र पर 60° का कोण अंतरित करती है। यदि वृत्त की त्रिज्या 10 cm है, तो जीवा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 cm"},"2":{"en":"10 cm"},"3":{"en":"15 cm"},"4":{"en":"20 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M69 185L111 111L154 185M69 185L154 185M103 125A16 16 0 0 0 119 125\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"85\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"111\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"105\">O</text><text x=\"61\" y=\"201\">A</text><text x=\"161\" y=\"201\">B</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"147\">10</text></g></svg><br>The two radii and the chord form an isosceles triangle with vertex angle 60°<br>So it is an equilateral triangle<br>Chord \\(=\\) radius \\(= \\boxed{10\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 10 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M69 185L111 111L154 185M69 185L154 185M103 125A16 16 0 0 0 119 125\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"85\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"111\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"105\">O</text><text x=\"61\" y=\"201\">A</text><text x=\"161\" y=\"201\">B</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"147\">10</text></g></svg><br>दो त्रिज्याएँ और जीवा मिलकर 60° शीर्ष कोण वाला समद्विबाहु त्रिभुज बनाते हैं<br>अतः यह समबाहु त्रिभुज है<br>जीवा \\(=\\) त्रिज्या \\(= \\boxed{10\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 10 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000072241","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"In a quadrilateral ABCD, the diagonal AC is 20 cm. The perpendiculars from vertices B and D to AC are 9 cm and 11 cm respectively. Find the area of ABCD. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"चतुर्भुज ABCD में विकर्ण AC = 20 cm है। शीर्षों B और D से AC पर डाले गए लंब क्रमशः 9 cm और 11 cm हैं। ABCD का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"180 cm²"},"2":{"en":"200 cm²"},"3":{"en":"220 cm²"},"4":{"en":"240 cm²"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"212\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 212 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 98L122 26L186 98L82 186ZM26 98L186 98M128 98L128 92L122 92M76 98L76 104L82 104\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M122 26L122 98M82 186L82 98\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"10\" y=\"102\">A</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"16\">B</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"102\">C</text><text x=\"79\" y=\"204\">D</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"66\">9 cm</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"146\">11 cm</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11\">AC = 20 cm</text></g></svg><br>Area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times AC \\times (h_1 + h_2)\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 20 \\times (9 + 11) = 10 \\times 20\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{200\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 200 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"212\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 212 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 98L122 26L186 98L82 186ZM26 98L186 98M128 98L128 92L122 92M76 98L76 104L82 104\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M122 26L122 98M82 186L82 98\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"10\" y=\"102\">A</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"16\">B</text><text x=\"202\" y=\"102\">C</text><text x=\"79\" y=\"204\">D</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"66\">9 cm</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"146\">11 cm</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11\">AC = 20 cm</text></g></svg><br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times AC \\times (h_1 + h_2)\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 20 \\times (9 + 11) = 10 \\times 20\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{200\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 200 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000072242","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate the following expression:<br><br>\\(\\left(\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1 + \\cos\\theta} + \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta}\\right)\\) [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित व्यंजक का मान ज्ञात कीजिए:<br><br>\\(\\left(\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1 + \\cos\\theta} + \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta}\\right)\\) [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2 sin θ"},"2":{"en":"2 tan θ"},"3":{"en":"tan θ"},"4":{"en":"2 cos θ"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"First bracket: \\(\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta + (1 + \\cos\\theta)^2}{\\sin\\theta(1 + \\cos\\theta)} = \\frac{2 + 2\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta(1 + \\cos\\theta)} = \\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta}\\)<br>Second bracket: \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta} = \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\)<br>Product \\(= \\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta} \\times \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\boxed{2\\cos\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2 cos θ.</b>","hi":"पहला कोष्ठक: \\(\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta + (1 + \\cos\\theta)^2}{\\sin\\theta(1 + \\cos\\theta)} = \\frac{2 + 2\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta(1 + \\cos\\theta)} = \\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta}\\)<br>दूसरा कोष्ठक: \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta} = \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\)<br>गुणनफल \\(= \\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta} \\times \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\boxed{2\\cos\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 2 cos θ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000072243","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The base of a prism is a right-angled isosceles triangle whose hypotenuse is \\(5\\sqrt{2}\\) cm. If the height of the prism is 10 cm, find the volume of the prism. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक प्रिज़्म का आधार समकोण समद्विबाहु त्रिभुज है जिसका कर्ण \\(5\\sqrt{2}\\) cm है। यदि प्रिज़्म की ऊँचाई 10 cm है, तो प्रिज़्म का आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"110 cm³"},"2":{"en":"125 cm³"},"3":{"en":"150 cm³"},"4":{"en":"135 cm³"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"146\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"-21 0 146 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 196L99 196M26 49L99 49M26 196L26 49M99 49L63 26M99 196L99 49M63 26L26 49\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M99 196L63 173M63 173L26 196M63 173L63 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"0\" y=\"127\">10 cm</text><text x=\"63\" y=\"212\">a</text><text x=\"37\" y=\"177\">a</text></g></svg><br>Equal sides: \\(2a^2 = (5\\sqrt{2})^2 = 50 \\Rightarrow a = 5\\) cm<br>Base area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 5 = 12.5\\) cm²<br>Volume \\(= 12.5 \\times 10 = \\boxed{125\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 125 cm³.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"146\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"-21 0 146 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 196L99 196M26 49L99 49M26 196L26 49M99 49L63 26M99 196L99 49M63 26L26 49\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M99 196L63 173M63 173L26 196M63 173L63 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"0\" y=\"127\">10 cm</text><text x=\"63\" y=\"212\">a</text><text x=\"37\" y=\"177\">a</text></g></svg><br>बराबर भुजाएँ: \\(2a^2 = (5\\sqrt{2})^2 = 50 \\Rightarrow a = 5\\) cm<br>आधार क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 5 = 12.5\\) cm²<br>आयतन \\(= 12.5 \\times 10 = \\boxed{125\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 125 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000072244","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Solve: \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9} - \\sqrt{8}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6}}\\) [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"हल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9} - \\sqrt{8}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6}}\\) [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(3 + \\sqrt{6}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(3 - \\sqrt{6}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(3 + \\sqrt{5}\\)"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Rationalising each term: \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9} - \\sqrt{8}} = \\sqrt{9} + \\sqrt{8}\\), etc.<br>\\(= (\\sqrt{9} + \\sqrt{8}) - (\\sqrt{8} + \\sqrt{7}) + (\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{6})\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{9} + \\sqrt{6} = 3 + \\sqrt{6}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3 + \\sqrt{6}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(3 + \\sqrt{6}\\).</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद का परिमेयकरण: \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9} - \\sqrt{8}} = \\sqrt{9} + \\sqrt{8}\\) इत्यादि<br>\\(= (\\sqrt{9} + \\sqrt{8}) - (\\sqrt{8} + \\sqrt{7}) + (\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{6})\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{9} + \\sqrt{6} = 3 + \\sqrt{6}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3 + \\sqrt{6}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(3 + \\sqrt{6}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000072245","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, points D and E lie on side BC such that AD = AE and ∠BAD = ∠EAC. If AB = (3x + 1) cm, BD = 9 cm, AC = 34 cm, and EC = (y + 1) cm, then find the value of (x + y). [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, बिंदु D और E भुजा BC पर इस प्रकार स्थित हैं कि AD = AE और ∠BAD = ∠EAC है। यदि AB = (3x + 1) cm, BD = 9 cm, AC = 34 cm और EC = (y + 1) cm है, तो (x + y) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11"},"2":{"en":"12"},"3":{"en":"16"},"4":{"en":"19"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"205\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 205\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M141 26L26 179L256 179ZM141 26L103 179M141 26L179 179M127 104l-10 -2M165 101l-10 2\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"141\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"189\">B</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"189\">C</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"190\">D</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"190\">E</text><text x=\"63\" y=\"91\">3x + 1</text><text x=\"211\" y=\"97\">34</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"11\">9</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"11\">y + 1</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\triangle ABD \\cong \\triangle ACE\\) (AD = AE, ∠BAD = ∠EAC, and \\(\\angle ADB = \\angle AEC\\) since AD = AE)<br>So AB = AC and BD = EC<br>\\(3x + 1 = 34 \\Rightarrow x = 11\\) and \\(y + 1 = 9 \\Rightarrow y = 8\\)<br>\\(x + y = 11 + 8 = \\boxed{19}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 19.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"205\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 205\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M141 26L26 179L256 179ZM141 26L103 179M141 26L179 179M127 104l-10 -2M165 101l-10 2\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"141\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"189\">B</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"189\">C</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"190\">D</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"190\">E</text><text x=\"63\" y=\"91\">3x + 1</text><text x=\"211\" y=\"97\">34</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"11\">9</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"11\">y + 1</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\triangle ABD \\cong \\triangle ACE\\) (AD = AE, ∠BAD = ∠EAC, तथा AD = AE से \\(\\angle ADB = \\angle AEC\\))<br>अतः AB = AC और BD = EC<br>\\(3x + 1 = 34 \\Rightarrow x = 11\\) और \\(y + 1 = 9 \\Rightarrow y = 8\\)<br>\\(x + y = 11 + 8 = \\boxed{19}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 19 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000072246","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Read the following frequency polygon which represents class interval (Living Area (Square Meters)) on the x-axis and frequency (Number of Units Sold) on the y-axis, and answer the following question:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q66.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If the median apartment size is defined as the interval containing the middle unit, which interval is the median class? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित बारंबारता बहुभुज पढ़िए जिसमें x-अक्ष पर वर्ग अंतराल (रहने का क्षेत्रफल (वर्ग मीटर)) और y-अक्ष पर बारंबारता (बेची गई इकाइयों की संख्या) है, और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q66.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि माध्यक अपार्टमेंट आकार को मध्य इकाई वाले अंतराल के रूप में परिभाषित किया जाए, तो माध्यक वर्ग कौन-सा अंतराल है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"60–80 sq m","hi":"60–80 वर्ग मीटर"},"2":{"en":"100–120 sq m","hi":"100–120 वर्ग मीटर"},"3":{"en":"80–100 sq m","hi":"80–100 वर्ग मीटर"},"4":{"en":"120–140 sq m","hi":"120–140 वर्ग मीटर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"From the polygon: 20–40 → 0, 40–60 → 22, 60–80 → 42, 80–100 → 60, 100–120 → 37, 120–140 → 21, 140–160 → 7, 160–180 → 0<br>Total units \\(= 189\\), so the median unit is the 95th<br>Cumulative: 0, 22, 64, 124 → the 95th unit lies in 80–100<br>Median class \\(= \\boxed{80\\text{–}100\\ \\text{sq m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 80–100 sq m.</b>","hi":"बहुभुज से: 20–40 → 0, 40–60 → 22, 60–80 → 42, 80–100 → 60, 100–120 → 37, 120–140 → 21, 140–160 → 7, 160–180 → 0<br>कुल इकाइयाँ \\(= 189\\), अतः माध्यक इकाई 95वीं है<br>संचयी: 0, 22, 64, 124 → 95वीं इकाई 80–100 में है<br>माध्यक वर्ग \\(= \\boxed{80\\text{–}100\\ \\text{sq m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 80–100 वर्ग मीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q66.jpg"]}},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000072247","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles of radii 25 cm and 17 cm intersect such that the length of their common chord is 30 cm. Find the distance between the centers of the two circles, given that the centers lie on opposite sides of the chord. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"25 cm और 17 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो वृत्त इस प्रकार प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं कि उनकी उभयनिष्ठ जीवा की लंबाई 30 cm है। दोनों वृत्तों के केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए, यदि केंद्र जीवा के विपरीत ओर स्थित हैं। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 cm"},"2":{"en":"21 cm"},"3":{"en":"24 cm"},"4":{"en":"28 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M179 60L179 162M111 111L179 60M206 111L179 60M185 111L185 105L179 105\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M111 111L206 111\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"85\"/><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"111\" r=\"58\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"111\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"103\" y=\"122\">A</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"122\">B</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"57\">P</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"173\">Q</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"11\">M</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"82\">25</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"85\">17</text><text x=\"184\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">15</text></g></svg><br>Half chord \\(= 15\\) cm; each centre is at distance \\(\\sqrt{r^2 - 15^2}\\) from the chord<br>First circle: \\(\\sqrt{625 - 225} = 20\\) cm; second: \\(\\sqrt{289 - 225} = 8\\) cm<br>Since the centres are on opposite sides, distance \\(= 20 + 8 = \\boxed{28\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 28 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M179 60L179 162M111 111L179 60M206 111L179 60M185 111L185 105L179 105\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M111 111L206 111\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"85\"/><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"111\" r=\"58\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"111\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"111\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"103\" y=\"122\">A</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"122\">B</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"57\">P</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"173\">Q</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"11\">M</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"82\">25</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"85\">17</text><text x=\"184\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">15</text></g></svg><br>आधी जीवा \\(= 15\\) cm; प्रत्येक केंद्र जीवा से \\(\\sqrt{r^2 - 15^2}\\) दूरी पर है<br>पहला वृत्त: \\(\\sqrt{625 - 225} = 20\\) cm; दूसरा: \\(\\sqrt{289 - 225} = 8\\) cm<br>केंद्र विपरीत ओर हैं, अतः दूरी \\(= 20 + 8 = \\boxed{28\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 28 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000072248","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Study the given histogram that shows the height (in cm) of 100 students in an athletic team and answer the question that follows:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q68.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If 10 students from the 170–180 group shift to 150–160, which becomes the new modal class? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिया गया आयतचित्र, जो एक एथलेटिक टीम के 100 विद्यार्थियों की ऊँचाई (cm में) दर्शाता है, का अध्ययन कीजिए और आगे दिए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q68.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि 170–180 समूह के 10 विद्यार्थी 150–160 में चले जाएँ, तो नया बहुलक वर्ग कौन-सा हो जाएगा? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"150-160"},"2":{"en":"160-170"},"3":{"en":"170-180"},"4":{"en":"180-190"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Frequencies: 140–150 → 4, 150–160 → 8, 160–170 → 16, 170–180 → 30, 180–190 → 22, 190–200 → 14, 200–210 → 6<br>After shifting 10 students: 150–160 \\(\\to 18\\), 170–180 \\(\\to 20\\)<br>Highest frequency is now 22, in 180–190<br>New modal class \\(= \\boxed{180\\text{-}190}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 180-190.</b>","hi":"बारंबारताएँ: 140–150 → 4, 150–160 → 8, 160–170 → 16, 170–180 → 30, 180–190 → 22, 190–200 → 14, 200–210 → 6<br>10 विद्यार्थी स्थानांतरित होने पर: 150–160 \\(\\to 18\\), 170–180 \\(\\to 20\\)<br>अब अधिकतम बारंबारता 22 है, जो 180–190 में है<br>नया बहुलक वर्ग \\(= \\boxed{180\\text{-}190}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 180-190 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q68.jpg"]}},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000072249","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A can contains a mixture of two liquids P and Q in the ratio 8:7. If 5 liters of the mixture is taken out and the remaining part of the can is filled with Q, then the ratio of P and Q becomes 2:3. Find how many liters of liquid P was there in the can initially? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक कैन में दो द्रवों P और Q का मिश्रण 8:7 के अनुपात में है। यदि 5 लीटर मिश्रण निकाल लिया जाए और कैन का शेष भाग Q से भर दिया जाए, तो P और Q का अनुपात 2:3 हो जाता है। प्रारंभ में कैन में द्रव P कितने लीटर था? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{17}{3}\\) liters","hi":"\\(\\frac{17}{3}\\) लीटर"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{22}{3}\\) liters","hi":"\\(\\frac{22}{3}\\) लीटर"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{28}{3}\\) liters","hi":"\\(\\frac{28}{3}\\) लीटर"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{32}{3}\\) liters","hi":"\\(\\frac{32}{3}\\) लीटर"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let the mixture be \\(15k\\) litres, so P \\(= 8k\\), Q \\(= 7k\\)<br>Removing 5 L removes \\(\\frac{8}{15} \\times 5 = \\frac{8}{3}\\) L of P; P left \\(= 8k - \\frac{8}{3}\\)<br>Remaining Q \\(= 7k - \\frac{7}{3}\\); adding 5 L of Q gives \\(7k - \\frac{7}{3} + 5 = 7k + \\frac{8}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{8k - 8/3}{7k + 8/3} = \\frac{2}{3} \\Rightarrow 24k - 8 = 14k + \\frac{16}{3} \\Rightarrow 10k = \\frac{40}{3} \\Rightarrow k = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>P \\(= 8k = \\frac{32}{3}\\) litres \\(= \\boxed{\\frac{32}{3}\\ \\text{liters}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{32}{3}\\) liters.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए मिश्रण \\(15k\\) लीटर है, अतः P \\(= 8k\\), Q \\(= 7k\\)<br>5 लीटर निकालने पर \\(\\frac{8}{15} \\times 5 = \\frac{8}{3}\\) लीटर P निकलता है; P शेष \\(= 8k - \\frac{8}{3}\\)<br>शेष Q \\(= 7k - \\frac{7}{3}\\); 5 लीटर Q मिलाने पर \\(7k - \\frac{7}{3} + 5 = 7k + \\frac{8}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{8k - 8/3}{7k + 8/3} = \\frac{2}{3} \\Rightarrow 24k - 8 = 14k + \\frac{16}{3} \\Rightarrow 10k = \\frac{40}{3} \\Rightarrow k = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>P \\(= 8k = \\frac{32}{3}\\) लीटर \\(= \\boxed{\\frac{32}{3}\\ \\text{liters}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{32}{3}\\) लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000072250","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If the radius of a right circular cylinder is tripled and the height is one-third, then find the ratio between the new volume and the previous volume of the cylinder? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि एक लंब वृत्तीय बेलन की त्रिज्या तीन गुनी और ऊँचाई एक-तिहाई कर दी जाए, तो बेलन के नए आयतन और पिछले आयतन के बीच अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 : 3"},"2":{"en":"9 : 1"},"3":{"en":"3 : 1"},"4":{"en":"1 : 9"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Volume \\(= \\pi r^2 h\\)<br>New volume \\(= \\pi (3r)^2 \\frac{h}{3} = 3\\pi r^2 h\\)<br>Ratio \\(= 3\\pi r^2 h : \\pi r^2 h = \\boxed{3 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3 : 1.</b>","hi":"आयतन \\(= \\pi r^2 h\\)<br>नया आयतन \\(= \\pi (3r)^2 \\frac{h}{3} = 3\\pi r^2 h\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= 3\\pi r^2 h : \\pi r^2 h = \\boxed{3 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 : 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000072251","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper marks the price of an article 25% above its cost price. He gives a discount of 10% on the marked price. Find his profit percentage. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक दुकानदार किसी वस्तु का मूल्य उसके क्रय मूल्य से 25% अधिक अंकित करता है। वह अंकित मूल्य पर 10% छूट देता है। उसका लाभ प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10.5%"},"2":{"en":"15%"},"3":{"en":"12.5%"},"4":{"en":"17%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let CP \\(= 100\\), MP \\(= 125\\)<br>SP \\(= 125 \\times 0.90 = 112.5\\)<br>Profit \\(= \\frac{12.5}{100} \\times 100 = \\boxed{12.5\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12.5%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए क्रय मूल्य \\(= 100\\), अंकित मूल्य \\(= 125\\)<br>विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 125 \\times 0.90 = 112.5\\)<br>लाभ \\(= \\frac{12.5}{100} \\times 100 = \\boxed{12.5\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12.5% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000072252","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart presents the percentage distribution of different forest types within a specific geographical area. Analyze the data provided and answer the following question based on the chart.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What is the total combined central angle (in degrees) formed at the center for the Tropical Evergreen and Alpine sectors? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित पाई-चार्ट एक विशिष्ट भौगोलिक क्षेत्र में विभिन्न वन प्रकारों के प्रतिशत वितरण को दर्शाता है। दिए गए आँकड़ों का विश्लेषण कीजिए और चार्ट के आधार पर निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Tropical Evergreen और Alpine क्षेत्रों के लिए केंद्र पर बनने वाला कुल संयुक्त केंद्रीय कोण (डिग्री में) क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"162°"},"2":{"en":"174°"},"3":{"en":"150°"},"4":{"en":"148°"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the pie chart: Tropical Evergreen = 30%, Alpine = 15%<br>Combined share \\(= 45\\%\\)<br>Central angle \\(= \\frac{45}{100} \\times 360° = \\boxed{162°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 162°.</b>","hi":"पाई चार्ट से: Tropical Evergreen = 30%, Alpine = 15%<br>संयुक्त हिस्सा \\(= 45\\%\\)<br>केंद्रीय कोण \\(= \\frac{45}{100} \\times 360° = \\boxed{162°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 162° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q72.jpg"]}},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000072253","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"From a point on the ground, the angle of elevation of the top of a tower is 30°. After walking 40 m towards the tower, the angle of elevation becomes 60°. Find the height of the tower. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भूमि पर स्थित एक बिंदु से एक मीनार के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण 30° है। मीनार की ओर 40 m चलने पर उन्नयन कोण 60° हो जाता है। मीनार की ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(20\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"2":{"en":"\\(10\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"3":{"en":"\\(30\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"4":{"en":"\\(40\\sqrt{3}\\) m"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L256 159M26 159L26 26M34 159L34 151L26 151M103 159L26 26M85 159A18 18 0 0 1 94 143M256 159L26 26M238 159A18 18 0 0 1 240 150\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"170\">B</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"96\">h</text><text x=\"77\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"173\">C</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"256\" y=\"173\">D</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"175\">x</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"175\">40 m</text></g></svg><br>Let the height be \\(h\\) and the nearer distance be \\(x\\)<br>\\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h}{x} \\Rightarrow h = x\\sqrt{3}\\); \\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{x + 40}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{x\\sqrt{3}}{x + 40} \\Rightarrow x + 40 = 3x \\Rightarrow x = 20\\)<br>\\(h = 20\\sqrt{3}\\) m \\(= \\boxed{20\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(20\\sqrt{3}\\) m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 159L256 159M26 159L26 26M34 159L34 151L26 151M103 159L26 26M85 159A18 18 0 0 1 94 143M256 159L26 26M238 159A18 18 0 0 1 240 150\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"170\">B</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"96\">h</text><text x=\"77\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"173\">C</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"256\" y=\"173\">D</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"175\">x</text><text x=\"179\" y=\"175\">40 m</text></g></svg><br>मान लीजिए ऊँचाई \\(h\\) और निकट की दूरी \\(x\\) है<br>\\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h}{x} \\Rightarrow h = x\\sqrt{3}\\); \\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{x + 40}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{x\\sqrt{3}}{x + 40} \\Rightarrow x + 40 = 3x \\Rightarrow x = 20\\)<br>\\(h = 20\\sqrt{3}\\) m \\(= \\boxed{20\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(20\\sqrt{3}\\) m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000072254","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"What is the average of the first 20 positive multiples of 7? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"7 के प्रथम 20 धनात्मक गुणजों का औसत क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"70.5"},"2":{"en":"71.5"},"3":{"en":"73.5"},"4":{"en":"77"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The first 20 multiples are \\(7, 14, \\dots, 140\\) (an AP)<br>Average \\(= \\frac{7 + 140}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{147}{2} = \\boxed{73.5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 73.5.</b>","hi":"प्रथम 20 गुणज \\(7, 14, \\dots, 140\\) हैं (एक समांतर श्रेढ़ी)<br>औसत \\(= \\frac{7 + 140}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{147}{2} = \\boxed{73.5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 73.5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000072255","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"An automobile manufacturer tracks the production of Electric Vehicles (EVs) and Internal Combustion Engine (ICE) vehicles over three consecutive years. The relevant data is illustrated in the bar graph given below:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>In which year did the production of EVs make up more than 35% of the total vehicle production (EV + ICE vehicles), and what is the percentage value rounded to two decimal places? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक ऑटोमोबाइल निर्माता लगातार तीन वर्षों में इलेक्ट्रिक वाहनों (EV) और इंटरनल कंबशन इंजन (ICE) वाहनों के उत्पादन पर नज़र रखता है। संबंधित आँकड़े नीचे दिए बार ग्राफ में दर्शाए गए हैं:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>किस वर्ष EV का उत्पादन कुल वाहन उत्पादन (EV + ICE वाहन) का 35% से अधिक हुआ, और दो दशमलव स्थानों तक पूर्णांकित प्रतिशत मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2024, 33.33%"},"2":{"en":"2025, 46.32%"},"3":{"en":"2025, 48.28%"},"4":{"en":"2023, 36.25%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"From the bar graph: 2023 → EV 40, ICE 160; 2024 → EV 70, ICE 140; 2025 → EV 112, ICE 120<br>2023: \\(\\frac{40}{200} = 20\\%\\); 2024: \\(\\frac{70}{210} = 33.33\\%\\); 2025: \\(\\frac{112}{232} = 48.28\\%\\)<br>Only 2025 crosses 35%<br>\\(= \\boxed{2025,\\ 48.28\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2025, 48.28%.</b>","hi":"बार ग्राफ से: 2023 → EV 40, ICE 160; 2024 → EV 70, ICE 140; 2025 → EV 112, ICE 120<br>2023: \\(\\frac{40}{200} = 20\\%\\); 2024: \\(\\frac{70}{210} = 33.33\\%\\); 2025: \\(\\frac{112}{232} = 48.28\\%\\)<br>केवल 2025 में 35% से अधिक है<br>\\(= \\boxed{2025,\\ 48.28\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2025, 48.28% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg"]}}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000072256","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"<b>Select the wrongly spelt word out of the four alternatives.</b> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Prejudise"},"2":{"en":"Ignorant"},"3":{"en":"Repulsive"},"4":{"en":"Ancestor"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Prejudice (पूर्वाग्रह) = an unfair opinion formed without knowledge or reason.</b><br><b>Prejudise</b> is misspelt – the ending is '-dice', not '-dise'.<br><b>Ignorant (अज्ञानी)</b> = lacking knowledge – correct<br><b>Repulsive (घृणित)</b> = causing strong dislike – correct<br><b>Ancestor (पूर्वज)</b> = a person from whom one is descended – correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Prejudise.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000072257","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"<b>Select the wrongly spelt word out of the four alternatives.</b> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Anesthetic"},"2":{"en":"Intricate"},"3":{"en":"Unexpectid"},"4":{"en":"Creeping"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Unexpected (अप्रत्याशित) = not expected or foreseen.</b><br><b>Unexpectid</b> is misspelt – the ending is '-ed', not '-id'.<br><b>Anesthetic (निश्चेतक)</b> = a substance that causes loss of sensation – correct (US spelling)<br><b>Intricate (जटिल)</b> = very complicated or detailed – correct<br><b>Creeping (रेंगता हुआ)</b> = moving slowly and quietly – correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Unexpectid.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000072258","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.</b><br><br>The professor was known for his <b><u>abstruse</u></b> lecturing style. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Complex"},"2":{"en":"Simple"},"3":{"en":"Recondite"},"4":{"en":"Obscure"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Abstruse (दुर्बोध) = difficult to understand.</b><br><b>Simple (सरल)</b> = easy to understand ✔<br><b>Complex (जटिल)</b> = complicated – synonym<br><b>Recondite (गूढ़)</b> = little known, obscure – synonym<br><b>Obscure (अस्पष्ट)</b> = not clear – synonym<br>More antonyms: lucid, clear, plain.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Simple.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000072259","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.</b><br><br>His speech was marred by a certain <b><u>infelicity</u></b> of expression that confused the audience. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Unhappiness"},"2":{"en":"Appropriateness"},"3":{"en":"Misfortune"},"4":{"en":"Awkwardness"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Infelicity (अनुपयुक्तता) = an unsuitable or inappropriate expression or remark.</b><br><b>Appropriateness (उपयुक्तता)</b> = being suitable or proper ✔<br><b>Unhappiness (दुख)</b> = sadness – an older sense of infelicity, not opposite<br><b>Misfortune (दुर्भाग्य)</b> = bad luck – close to infelicity, not opposite<br><b>Awkwardness (भद्दापन)</b> = clumsiness – synonym<br>More antonyms: aptness, suitability, felicity.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Appropriateness.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000072260","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"<b>Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.</b><br><br>The gardens are <b><u>perenially</u></b> beautiful and lush. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Perennially"},"2":{"en":"Perenially"},"3":{"en":"Perenialy"},"4":{"en":"Perennialy"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Perennially (सदा, बारहमासी रूप से) = constantly; throughout the year.</b><br>Spelling: pere-<b>nn</b>-ia-<b>ll</b>y, double 'n' and double 'l'.<br><b>Perenially</b> – single 'n'<br><b>Perenialy</b> – single 'n' and single 'l'<br><b>Perennialy</b> – single 'l'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Perennially.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000072261","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"<b>Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.</b><br><br>The climate there is very <b><u>salubrius.</u></b> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Salubrious"},"2":{"en":"Salubrius"},"3":{"en":"Salubreeous"},"4":{"en":"Salubreous"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Salubrious (स्वास्थ्यप्रद) = good for health; pleasant.</b><br>Spelling: salubr-<b>i</b>-<b>ous</b>.<br><b>Salubrius</b> – 'o' missing in '-ious'<br><b>Salubreeous</b> – 'ee' in place of 'i'<br><b>Salubreous</b> – 'e' in place of 'i'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Salubrious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000072262","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named P, Q, R, and S. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.</b><br><br><b>1. Lack of sleep</b><br>P. and negatively affects<br>Q. not only impairs<br>R. but also weakens<br>S. cognitive functions<br><b>6. the immune system.</b> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PQRS"},"2":{"en":"RQSP"},"3":{"en":"QSRP"},"4":{"en":"SQRP"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QSRP</b><br><b>Q</b> 'not only impairs' follows the subject 'Lack of sleep' and gives the verb.<br><b>S</b> 'cognitive functions' is the object of 'impairs'.<br><b>R</b> 'but also weakens' completes the pair 'not only … but also'.<br><b>P</b> 'and negatively affects' leads to the last part 'the immune system'.<br>Lack of sleep not only impairs cognitive functions but also weakens and negatively affects the immune system.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): QSRP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000072263","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named P, Q, R, and S. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.</b><br><br><b>1. If we do not</b><br>P. of our natural resources<br>Q. take immediate steps<br>R. then future generations<br>S. for the conservation<br><b>6. will have to face severe crises.</b> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QSPR"},"2":{"en":"PSQR"},"3":{"en":"QRPS"},"4":{"en":"RSQP"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QSPR</b><br><b>Q</b> 'take immediate steps' completes the verb after 'If we do not'.<br><b>S</b> 'for the conservation' tells the purpose of the steps.<br><b>P</b> 'of our natural resources' completes 'conservation of…'.<br><b>R</b> 'then future generations' begins the result clause and joins part 6.<br>If we do not take immediate steps for the conservation of our natural resources, then future generations will have to face severe crises.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QSPR.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000072264","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the most appropriate option to fill the blank in the given sentence.</b><br><br>When the lights went out, we spent a ______ evening talking by the ______ light of a few candles. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"noiseless, waving"},"2":{"en":"silent, blinking"},"3":{"en":"quiet, flickering"},"4":{"en":"still, shaking"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Choose words that collocate naturally with the nouns – 'a quiet evening' and 'flickering light'.</b><br><b>Quiet (शांत)</b> evening is the natural phrase for a calm evening spent talking.<br><b>Flickering (टिमटिमाती)</b> = burning unsteadily – the usual word for candlelight.<br>Correct sentence: …we spent a <b>quiet</b> evening talking by the <b>flickering</b> light of a few candles.<br>noiseless, waving – 'waving light' is not idiomatic<br>silent, blinking – a 'silent evening' does not suit people talking; 'blinking' is used for lights going on and off<br>still, shaking – 'shaking light' is not used for candles<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): quiet, flickering.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000072265","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the most appropriate option to fill the blank in the given sentence.</b><br><br>This year’s costumes are ______ than last year's, but they were also ______ to prepare. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"elaborater, difficulter"},"2":{"en":"most elaborate, most difficult"},"3":{"en":"elaborate, difficult"},"4":{"en":"more elaborate, more difficult"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'than' needs the comparative degree; long adjectives form it with 'more'.</b><br>'Elaborate' and 'difficult' have three or more syllables, so: more elaborate, more difficult.<br>Correct sentence: This year's costumes are <b>more elaborate</b> than last year's, but they were also <b>more difficult</b> to prepare.<br>elaborater, difficulter – '-er' is not added to long adjectives<br>most elaborate, most difficult – superlative cannot be used with 'than'<br>elaborate, difficult – positive degree cannot be used with 'than'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): more elaborate, more difficult.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000072266","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"From the given options, select the homonym that corresponds to both Definition (P) and Definition (Q).<br><br>(P) A company's legal financial debts or monetary obligations owed to outside parties<br><br>(Q) A person or thing whose presence or behaviour creates a disadvantageous burden [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Liability"},"2":{"en":"Arrears"},"3":{"en":"Onus"},"4":{"en":"Impediment"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Liability (देनदारी; बोझ) has both meanings.</b><br>(P) In accounting, liabilities are a company's debts and obligations.<br>(Q) A person or thing that causes trouble is called a liability: 'The injured player became a liability to the team.'<br><b>Arrears (बकाया)</b> = money overdue – fits only (P)<br><b>Onus (दायित्व)</b> = responsibility or duty – fits neither fully<br><b>Impediment (बाधा)</b> = an obstacle – fits only (Q)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Liability.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000072267","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Which of the following options most accurately expresses the meaning of the idiom “to hit a purple patch”? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To experience a highly volatile period of civil unrest and institutional friction triggered by sudden austerity measures."},"2":{"en":"To enjoy an extended, highly successful period of outstanding performance, immense creativity, or exceptional good fortune."},"3":{"en":"To navigate an ideological gridlock within a legislative body where opposing parties refuse to reach an equitable policy compromise."},"4":{"en":"To have been luckily allotted a highly fertile piece of agricultural land that consistently yields an exceptionally bountiful crop."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Hit a purple patch (सफलता का दौर आना) = to have a period of great success or good luck.</b><br>Example: The batsman hit a purple patch, scoring three centuries in a row.<br>Option 1 – civil unrest (अशांति) is a bad period, the opposite<br>Option 3 – political deadlock (गतिरोध) has nothing to do with the idiom<br>Option 4 – a literal reading about fertile land (उपजाऊ भूमि)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): To enjoy an extended, highly successful period of outstanding performance, immense creativity, or exceptional good fortune.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000072268","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Read the sentences below carefully and identify which one contains a grammatical or structural error.<br><br>(P) Professor Ali’s latest historical monograph is more comprehensive than concise, offering exhaustive archival data at the expense of brevity.<br><br>(Q) The lead prosecutor remarked that the defendant's sudden courtroom confession was ready than calculated, catching the entire defence team off guard. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only P"},"2":{"en":"Only Q"},"3":{"en":"Both P and Q"},"4":{"en":"Neither P nor Q"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: When two qualities of the same thing are compared, use 'more + adjective + than + adjective'.</b><br>(P) 'more comprehensive than concise' follows the rule – correct.<br>(Q) 'was ready than calculated' has 'than' without a comparative. It should be 'was <b>more ready</b> than calculated'.<br>So only Q contains an error.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only Q.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000072269","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Read the following sentences carefully and identify which one contains a grammatical or structural error.<br><br>(P) The department seeks an administrative director more capable of managing international logistics than of drafting internal fiscal policies.<br><br>(Q) A legal framework less adaptive to technological disruption than intent on preserving historical precedents will inevitably stifle industrial innovation. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only P"},"2":{"en":"Only Q"},"3":{"en":"Both P and Q"},"4":{"en":"Neither P nor Q"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: In a comparison of two qualities, both sides must be parallel in form.</b><br>(P) 'more capable of managing … than of drafting' – both sides take 'of + -ing'; correct.<br>(Q) 'less adaptive to … than intent on …' – two adjectives with their prepositions, and the subject 'A legal framework' agrees with 'will … stifle'; correct.<br>Neither sentence has an error.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither P nor Q.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000072270","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the following passive sentence into active voice. Select the option that correctly identifies the true actor and uses the appropriate active transitive verb.<br><br>A fierce exchange of mutual misunderstanding is generated by alternative ways of thinking and different systems of value, while the individual is left entirely trapped within a rigid, unforgiving worldview. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Alternative ways of thinking and different systems of value generate a fierce exchange of mutual misunderstanding, while a rigid, unforgiving worldview leaves the individual entirely trapped."},"2":{"en":"Alternative ways of thought and different systems of value generate a fierce exchange of mutual misunderstanding, while a rigid, unforgiving worldview leaves the individual entirely trapped."},"3":{"en":"Alternative ways of thought and different systems of value generate a fiery exchanged of mutual misunderstanding, while a rigid, unforgiving worldview leaves the individual entirely trapped."},"4":{"en":"Alternative ways of thinking and different systems of value generate a fierce exchange of mutual misunderstanding, while a rigid, unforgiving worldview leaving the individual entirely trapping."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple present passive (is + V3) → active: Agent + V1/V5 + Object.</b><br>Clause 1: the agent 'alternative ways of thinking and different systems of value' becomes the subject → generate a fierce exchange…<br>Clause 2: the worldview that traps the individual is the actor → a rigid, unforgiving worldview leaves the individual entirely trapped.<br>Option 2 – changes 'thinking' to 'thought'<br>Option 3 – 'thought' and 'a fiery exchanged' change the wording and grammar<br>Option 4 – 'leaving … trapping' leaves the clause without a finite verb<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Alternative ways of thinking and different systems of value generate a fierce exchange of mutual misunderstanding, while a rigid, unforgiving worldview leaves the individual entirely trapped.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000072271","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the statement that represents the indirect narration of the given direct narration.<br><br>Ritam said to Asha, “The local groups shouted at me, ‘You had better move away because we are not going to tolerate your relative's community activism regarding cultural heritage and migration!’” [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ritam told Asha that the local groups shouted at him that he had better move away because they were not going to tolerate his relative's community activism regarding cultural heritage and migration."},"2":{"en":"Ritam told Asha that the local groups shouted at him that he had better moved away because they were not going to tolerate his relative's community activism regarding cultural heritage and migration."},"3":{"en":"Ritam told Asha that the local groups had shouted at him that he had better been moving away because they were not going to tolerate his relative's community activism regarding cultural heritage and migration."},"4":{"en":"Ritam told Asha that the local groups had shouted at him that he had better move away because they were not going to tolerate his relative's community activism regarding cultural heritage and migration."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: said to → told; past reporting verb changes simple past to past perfect and 'are' to 'were'; 'had better + V1' does not change.</b><br>'shouted' → 'had shouted'; 'me' → 'him'; 'You' → 'he'; 'we are' → 'they were'; 'your' → 'his'.<br>Indirect: Ritam told Asha that the local groups <b>had shouted</b> at him that he <b>had better move</b> away because they were not going to tolerate his relative's community activism…<br>Option 1 – 'shouted' not changed to past perfect<br>Option 2 – 'had better moved' – had better takes V1<br>Option 3 – 'had better been moving' is wrong<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Ritam told Asha that the local groups had shouted at him that he had better move away because they were not going to tolerate his relative's community activism regarding cultural heritage and migration.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000072272","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the sentence below carefully. Choose the option (A/B/C) that best improves the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select Option D (No improvement required).<br><br>The planetary geologist hypothesised that ancient Martian liquid water could have fostered microbial life; consequently, early organic matter might still survive within deep subsurface caves today. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A hypothesis was made by the planetary geologist that if liquid water flowed on the ancient Martian surface, microbial life will have emerged, indicating that early organic matter will survive within deep subsurface caves today."},"2":{"en":"The planetary geologist hypothesised that if liquid water had flown on the ancient Martian surface, microbial life should have emerged – a possibility indicating that early organic matter might have survive within deep subsurface caves today."},"3":{"en":"According to the planetary geologist’s hypothesis, had ancient Martian liquid water fostered microbial life, consequently, early organic matter shall still be surviving within deep subsurface caves today."},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'could have + V3' expresses a past possibility; 'might + V1' expresses a present possibility.</b><br>'could have fostered' (past) and 'might still survive … today' (present) are correctly used and joined by '; consequently,'. The sentence needs no change.<br>Option 1 – 'flowed … will have emerged … will survive' mixes tenses and makes a guess sound certain<br>Option 2 – 'had flown' (should be 'flowed') and 'might have survive' (should be 'survived') are wrong<br>Option 3 – 'had … fostered' with 'consequently' is a broken conditional; 'shall still be surviving' is wrong<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): No improvement required.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000072273","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the sentence below carefully. Choose the option (A/B/C) that best improves the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select Option D (No improvement required).<br><br>The core reason why the global tech conglomerate decided to withdraw its investment from the region is because a massive supply chain disruption was suffered by its manufacturing division during the previous fiscal quarter. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The global tech conglomerate decided to withdraw its investment from the region because its manufacturing division suffered a massive supply chain disruption during the previous fiscal quarter."},"2":{"en":"The reason why the global tech conglomerate decided to withdraw its investment from the region was owing to its manufacturing division suffering a massive supply chain disruption during the previous fiscal quarter."},"3":{"en":"The global tech conglomerate decided on withdrawing its investment from the region on account of a massive supply chain disruption being suffered by its manufacturing division during the previous fiscal quarter."},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'The reason … is because' is redundant; use 'because' alone or 'The reason … is that'.</b><br>The original also uses a weak passive ('was suffered by'). Option 1 removes the redundancy and uses the active voice.<br>Improved: The global tech conglomerate decided to withdraw its investment from the region <b>because its manufacturing division suffered</b> a massive supply chain disruption…<br>Option 2 – 'The reason … was owing to' is still redundant<br>Option 3 – keeps the clumsy passive 'being suffered by'<br>Option 4 – the sentence has an error, so improvement is needed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The global tech conglomerate decided to withdraw its investment from the region because its manufacturing division suffered a massive supply chain disruption during the previous fiscal quarter.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000072274","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Select the correct passive form of the given sentence.</b><br><br>The board had already selected the new candidate before the announcement. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The new candidate was already selected by the board before the announcement."},"2":{"en":"The new candidate has already been selected by the board before the announcement."},"3":{"en":"The new candidate had already been selected by the board before the announcement."},"4":{"en":"The new candidate was being selected by the board before the announcement."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect active (had + V3) → passive: had + been + V3.</b><br>'the new candidate' becomes the subject; 'the board' becomes the agent.<br>Passive: The new candidate <b>had already been selected</b> by the board before the announcement.<br>Option 1 – simple past passive (was selected)<br>Option 2 – present perfect passive (has been selected)<br>Option 4 – past continuous passive (was being selected)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The new candidate had already been selected by the board before the announcement.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000072275","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"The following sentence is given in Indirect Speech. Select the option that correctly expresses it in Direct Speech.<br><br>Mr. Casaubon bluntly asked Dorothea whether she would faithfully continue compiling his sprawling, unfinished mythological notes after his death. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mr. Casaubon bluntly asked Dorothea, “whether she would faithfully continue compiling his sprawling, unfinished mythological notes after his death.”"},"2":{"en":"Mr. Casaubon bluntly said to Dorothea, “Will you faithfully continue compiling my sprawling, unfinished mythological notes after my death?”"},"3":{"en":"Mr. Casaubon bluntly told Dorothea, “Would you faithfully continue compiling my sprawling, unfinished mythological notes after my death!”"},"4":{"en":"Mr. Casaubon bluntly questioned Dorothea, “You will faithfully continue compiling my sprawling, unfinished mythological notes after my death?”"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'asked … whether' → said to, a yes/no question in inverted form with '?'; 'would' → 'will'; pronouns change back to the speaker's.</b><br>'she would' → 'Will you'; 'his notes' → 'my notes'; 'his death' → 'my death'.<br>Direct: Mr. Casaubon bluntly said to Dorothea, “<b>Will you</b> faithfully continue compiling <b>my</b> sprawling, unfinished mythological notes after <b>my</b> death?”<br>Option 1 – keeps 'whether' and the indirect pronouns inside quotes<br>Option 3 – 'Would' not changed to 'Will', and ends with '!'<br>Option 4 – statement word order with a question mark<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Mr. Casaubon bluntly said to Dorothea, “Will you faithfully continue compiling my sprawling, unfinished mythological notes after my death?”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000072276","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>The global transition toward renewable energy has become both an environmental and economic necessity. Nations investing in solar, wind, and green hydrogen technologies can reduce carbon emissions and strengthen energy security. However, the pace of transition varies because governments must balance environmental goals with financial realities. Policymakers are often required to (A) _____ substantial public investment against immediate fiscal constraints, a task that demands both political resolve and economic foresight.<br>Technological innovation has improved the efficiency of renewable systems; (B) _____, the intermittent nature of sunlight and wind continues to pose operational challenges for power grids. Energy storage solutions are promising, but their large-scale deployment depends on sustained research and affordable manufacturing. Experts also argue that renewable projects should not be evaluated solely on short-term costs but on the broader economic benefits they (C) _____ over several decades.<br>Public enthusiasm alone cannot guarantee success. Effective implementation requires governments, industries, researchers, and citizens to (D) _____ their efforts rather than pursuing isolated initiatives. Without such cooperation, even well-designed policies may fail to achieve their intended objectives. Ultimately, the renewable energy revolution will succeed only if societies remain committed to innovation while refusing to (E) _____ complacency in the face of evolving environmental challenges.<br><br><br>Fill in the blank (A) with the most appropriate word. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"weigh"},"2":{"en":"estimate"},"3":{"en":"measure"},"4":{"en":"fathom"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Policymakers are often required to (A) _____ substantial public investment against immediate fiscal constraints…\"</i><br>Grammar: the blank needs a base verb after 'to' that works with 'against'.<br>Meaning: <b>weigh A against B (तौलना, तुलना करना)</b> = compare two things to decide – policymakers balance investment against constraints.<br><b>Estimate (अनुमान लगाना)</b> – not used with 'against'<br><b>Measure (मापना)</b> – 'measure against' means compare to a standard, not balance two needs<br><b>Fathom (थाह पाना)</b> = understand deeply – does not fit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): weigh.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000072277","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>The global transition toward renewable energy has become both an environmental and economic necessity. Nations investing in solar, wind, and green hydrogen technologies can reduce carbon emissions and strengthen energy security. However, the pace of transition varies because governments must balance environmental goals with financial realities. Policymakers are often required to (A) _____ substantial public investment against immediate fiscal constraints, a task that demands both political resolve and economic foresight.<br>Technological innovation has improved the efficiency of renewable systems; (B) _____, the intermittent nature of sunlight and wind continues to pose operational challenges for power grids. Energy storage solutions are promising, but their large-scale deployment depends on sustained research and affordable manufacturing. Experts also argue that renewable projects should not be evaluated solely on short-term costs but on the broader economic benefits they (C) _____ over several decades.<br>Public enthusiasm alone cannot guarantee success. Effective implementation requires governments, industries, researchers, and citizens to (D) _____ their efforts rather than pursuing isolated initiatives. Without such cooperation, even well-designed policies may fail to achieve their intended objectives. Ultimately, the renewable energy revolution will succeed only if societies remain committed to innovation while refusing to (E) _____ complacency in the face of evolving environmental challenges.<br><br><br>Fill in the blank (B) with the most appropriate word. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"therefore"},"2":{"en":"moreover"},"3":{"en":"nevertheless"},"4":{"en":"consequently"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Technological innovation has improved the efficiency of renewable systems; (B) _____, the intermittent nature of sunlight and wind continues to pose operational challenges…\"</i><br>Grammar: a connector after a semicolon.<br>Meaning: improved efficiency and continuing challenges are in contrast, so <b>nevertheless (फिर भी)</b> fits.<br><b>Therefore (इसलिए)</b> – shows result, not contrast<br><b>Moreover (इसके अतिरिक्त)</b> – adds a similar point<br><b>Consequently (परिणामस्वरूप)</b> – shows result<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): nevertheless.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000072278","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>The global transition toward renewable energy has become both an environmental and economic necessity. Nations investing in solar, wind, and green hydrogen technologies can reduce carbon emissions and strengthen energy security. However, the pace of transition varies because governments must balance environmental goals with financial realities. Policymakers are often required to (A) _____ substantial public investment against immediate fiscal constraints, a task that demands both political resolve and economic foresight.<br>Technological innovation has improved the efficiency of renewable systems; (B) _____, the intermittent nature of sunlight and wind continues to pose operational challenges for power grids. Energy storage solutions are promising, but their large-scale deployment depends on sustained research and affordable manufacturing. Experts also argue that renewable projects should not be evaluated solely on short-term costs but on the broader economic benefits they (C) _____ over several decades.<br>Public enthusiasm alone cannot guarantee success. Effective implementation requires governments, industries, researchers, and citizens to (D) _____ their efforts rather than pursuing isolated initiatives. Without such cooperation, even well-designed policies may fail to achieve their intended objectives. Ultimately, the renewable energy revolution will succeed only if societies remain committed to innovation while refusing to (E) _____ complacency in the face of evolving environmental challenges.<br><br><br>Fill in the blank (C) with the most appropriate word. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"incur"},"2":{"en":"yield"},"3":{"en":"derive"},"4":{"en":"consume"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…on the broader economic benefits they (C) _____ over several decades.\"</i><br>Grammar: a verb with 'they' (renewable projects) as subject and 'benefits' as object.<br>Meaning: projects <b>yield (उत्पन्न करना, देना)</b> benefits.<br><b>Incur (उठाना)</b> – used for costs or losses, not benefits<br><b>Derive (प्राप्त करना)</b> – people derive benefits from projects; projects do not derive them<br><b>Consume (उपभोग करना)</b> – opposite sense<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): yield.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000072279","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>The global transition toward renewable energy has become both an environmental and economic necessity. Nations investing in solar, wind, and green hydrogen technologies can reduce carbon emissions and strengthen energy security. However, the pace of transition varies because governments must balance environmental goals with financial realities. Policymakers are often required to (A) _____ substantial public investment against immediate fiscal constraints, a task that demands both political resolve and economic foresight.<br>Technological innovation has improved the efficiency of renewable systems; (B) _____, the intermittent nature of sunlight and wind continues to pose operational challenges for power grids. Energy storage solutions are promising, but their large-scale deployment depends on sustained research and affordable manufacturing. Experts also argue that renewable projects should not be evaluated solely on short-term costs but on the broader economic benefits they (C) _____ over several decades.<br>Public enthusiasm alone cannot guarantee success. Effective implementation requires governments, industries, researchers, and citizens to (D) _____ their efforts rather than pursuing isolated initiatives. Without such cooperation, even well-designed policies may fail to achieve their intended objectives. Ultimately, the renewable energy revolution will succeed only if societies remain committed to innovation while refusing to (E) _____ complacency in the face of evolving environmental challenges.<br><br><br>Fill in the blank (D) with the most appropriate word. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"pool"},"2":{"en":"scatter"},"3":{"en":"divide"},"4":{"en":"withdraw"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Effective implementation requires governments, industries, researchers, and citizens to (D) _____ their efforts rather than pursuing isolated initiatives. Without such cooperation…\"</i><br>Meaning: 'rather than isolated initiatives' and 'such cooperation' show that efforts must be combined. <b>Pool (एकत्र करना)</b> = combine resources or efforts.<br><b>Scatter (बिखेरना)</b> – opposite of combining<br><b>Divide (बाँटना)</b> – separates efforts<br><b>Withdraw (वापस लेना)</b> – removes efforts<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): pool.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000072280","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words or phrases from the options given below.<br><br>The global transition toward renewable energy has become both an environmental and economic necessity. Nations investing in solar, wind, and green hydrogen technologies can reduce carbon emissions and strengthen energy security. However, the pace of transition varies because governments must balance environmental goals with financial realities. Policymakers are often required to (A) _____ substantial public investment against immediate fiscal constraints, a task that demands both political resolve and economic foresight.<br>Technological innovation has improved the efficiency of renewable systems; (B) _____, the intermittent nature of sunlight and wind continues to pose operational challenges for power grids. Energy storage solutions are promising, but their large-scale deployment depends on sustained research and affordable manufacturing. Experts also argue that renewable projects should not be evaluated solely on short-term costs but on the broader economic benefits they (C) _____ over several decades.<br>Public enthusiasm alone cannot guarantee success. Effective implementation requires governments, industries, researchers, and citizens to (D) _____ their efforts rather than pursuing isolated initiatives. Without such cooperation, even well-designed policies may fail to achieve their intended objectives. Ultimately, the renewable energy revolution will succeed only if societies remain committed to innovation while refusing to (E) _____ complacency in the face of evolving environmental challenges.<br><br><br>Fill in the blank (E) with the most appropriate phrase. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"succumb to"},"2":{"en":"aspire to"},"3":{"en":"adhere to"},"4":{"en":"resort to"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…while refusing to (E) _____ complacency in the face of evolving environmental challenges.\"</i><br>Meaning: societies must not give in to complacency. <b>Succumb to (के आगे झुक जाना)</b> = give way to a negative force.<br><b>Aspire to (आकांक्षा रखना)</b> – one aspires to something good, not complacency<br><b>Adhere to (पालन करना)</b> – used for rules or principles<br><b>Resort to (सहारा लेना)</b> – used for a course of action, not a state of mind<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): succumb to.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};